window.COURSE_QUESTION_BANK = {"data-structure":[{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:1","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الأول • سلايد 4","question":"Q1: What does an Abstract Data Type (ADT) primarily focus on?","options":["A) The exact number of bytes allocated in RAM.","B) WHAT operations are to be performed rather than HOW they are implemented.","C) The assembly language instructions generated by the compiler.","D) The physical disk sectors used for data storage."],"correct":1,"explanation":"نصت السلايد 4 صراحة على أن الـ ADT يركز على ما هي العمليات المطلوبة (WHAT operations are to be performed) وليس كيفية تنفيذها في الذاكرة (rather than HOW they are implemented).","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:2","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الأول • سلايد 8","question":"Q2: Which of the following is considered a characteristic of Primitive Data Types?","options":["A) They can store dynamic collections of mixed data.","B) They store a single value and are predefined by the language.","C) They require complex algorithms like recursion to traverse.","D) They are always implemented using pointers and linked structures."],"correct":1,"explanation":"نصت السلايد 8 على أن الأنواع الأولية (Primitive Data Types) تخزن قيمة مفردة واحدة فقط (Stores single values) وتكون معرفة مسبقاً داخل اللغة (Predefined by the language).","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:3","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الأول • سلايد 6","question":"Q3: The Stack ADT operates under which data access rule?","options":["A) FIFO (First In, First Out)","B) LIFO (Last In, First Out)","C) Random Access","D) Binary Search"],"correct":1,"explanation":"نصت السلايد 6 على أن المكدس (Stack) يعمل بقاعدة LIFO (Last In, First Out) أي أن آخر عنصر يدخل هو أول عنصر يخرج.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:4","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الأول • سلايد 5","question":"Q4: What is the main purpose of an Abstract Data Type (ADT) in software engineering?","options":["A) To eliminate the need for CPU memory.","B) To provide data abstraction by hiding implementation details from the user.","C) To force all data structures to use contiguous arrays.","D) To prevent the program from using primitive data types."],"correct":1,"explanation":"نصت السلايد 5 على أن الـ ADT يقدم وصفاً منطقياً ويوفر التجريد عبر إخفاء تفاصيل التنفيذ (ADT is a conceptual model; it hides the implementation details).","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:5","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الثاني • سلايد 12 و 14","question":"Q5: What is the primary characteristic that distinguishes a Linear Data Structure from a Non-Linear Data Structure according to Lecture 1?","options":["A) Linear structures use dynamic memory; Non-linear use static memory.","B) Linear structures arrange elements sequentially in a single level, while Non-linear structures arrange elements in multi-level hierarchies or networks.","C) Linear structures can only store integer types.","D) Non-linear structures can only be traversed using simple for loops."],"correct":1,"explanation":"نصت السلايد 12 و 14 على أن الهياكل الخطية ترتب العناصر بالتتابع في مستوى واحد (Single-level)، بينما الهياكل غير الخطية تتفرع وترتبط بعدة عناصر في مستويات هرمية أو شبكية (Multi-level).","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:6","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الثاني • سلايد 16","question":"Q6: In C++, how are elements of a standard one-dimensional array laid out in RAM?","options":["A) Non-contiguously across random heap fragments.","B) In contiguous (adjacent) memory locations with no gaps.","C) Inside CPU registers only.","D) Linked together using pointers."],"correct":1,"explanation":"نصت السلايد 16 صراحة على أن عناصر المصفوفة تُخزن في أماكن ذاكرة متصلة ومتجاورة بدون أي فواصل (stored in contiguous memory locations).","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:7","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الثاني • سلايد 16","question":"Q7: Why is accessing an element in an array by its index an O(1) operation?","options":["A) The CPU executes binary search on the array keys.","B) The physical memory address is calculated directly via an arithmetic formula: Base_Address + (index * Element_Size).","C) The compiler copies all array elements into the stack.","D) Array elements are sorted in ascending order automatically."],"correct":1,"explanation":"الوصول يأخذ زمناً ثابتاً O(1) لأن المعالج يحسب العنوان الفيزيائي مباشرة بالمعادلة الرياضية (Base_Address + index * Element_Size) ولا يحتاج للبحث.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:8","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الثاني • سلايد 16","question":"Q8: Given the declaration `int exams[5];`, what is the valid index range to access elements of this array in C++?","options":["A) 1 to 5","B) 0 to 4","C) 0 to 5","D) -1 to 4"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الفهرسة في لغة C++ تبدأ من 0، إذن لمصفوفة حجمها 5 تكون الفهارس المتاحة هي: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 (أي من 0 إلى SIZE - 1).","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:9","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الثالث • سلايد 29","question":"Q9: When passing a two-dimensional array to a function in C++, which dimension size is MANDATORY to include in the parameter list?","options":["A) The row dimension only.","B) The column dimension only.","C) Both row and column dimensions.","D) Neither dimension is needed."],"correct":1,"explanation":"نصت السلايد 29 صراحة على ترك قوس الصفوف فارغاً وتحديد حجم الأعمدة إجبارياً (Use empty [] for row, size declarator for column) حتى يتمكن المترجم من حساب عناوين الصفوف في الذاكرة.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:10","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الثالث • سلايد 28","question":"Q10: According to Lecture 1, what happens to array elements that are omitted during initialization, such as: `int exams[2][2] = {{84}, {92, 97}};`?","options":["A) They contain garbage values.","B) They cause a compilation syntax error.","C) They will automatically be set to 0 or NULL.","D) The program crashes at runtime."],"correct":2,"explanation":"نصت السلايد 28 صراحة على أن العناصر التي لا تُعطى قيمة ابتدائية تُضبط تلقائياً على صفر أو NULL (Array elements without initial values will be set to 0 or NULL).","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:11","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الثالث • سلايد 40","question":"Q11: Given the 3D array declaration `double timeGrid[3][4][5];`, what is the correct function prototype to accept this array as a parameter?","options":["A) void process(double [][][]);","B) void process(double [3][][]);","C) void process(double [][4][5]);","D) void process(double [3][4][]);"],"correct":2,"explanation":"نصت السلايد 40 على القاعدة: تحديد جميع الأبعاد ما عدا البُعد الأول فقط (specify all BUT the 1st dimension in prototype and header)؛ فنترك الأول فارغاً ونحدد [4][5].","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:12","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الثالث • سلايد 38","question":"Q12: To calculate the average score of each test (column by column) across all students, how should the nested loops be structured?","options":["A) Outer loop iterates over rows; inner loop iterates over columns.","B) Outer loop iterates over columns; inner loop iterates over rows.","C) Single loop from 0 to (ROWS * COLS).","D) Using recursion with two base cases."],"correct":1,"explanation":"لحساب كل عمود على حدة (سلايد 38)، نجعل حلقة الأعمدة (col) في الخارج ونصفر المجمع في بداية كل عمود، ونجعل حلقة الصفوف (row) في الداخل.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:13","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الرابع • سلايد 42","question":"Q13: What is the primary purpose of Templates in C++ according to Lecture 1?","options":["A) To speed up execution time using dynamic pointers.","B) To write generic and reusable code: \"Write once, use with different data types\".","C) To replace the need for arrays in linear memory.","D) To prevent functions from returning values."],"correct":1,"explanation":"نصت السلايد 42 صراحة على أن الغرض الأساسي من القوالب هو كتابة الكود مرة واحدة واستخدامه مع أنواع بيانات مختلفة (Write once, use with different data types).","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:14","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الرابع • سلايد 42","question":"Q14: Which of the following is NOT listed as a benefit of Templates in slide 42?","options":["A) Code reusability","B) Type safety","C) Runtime heap compression","D) Performance (compile-time resolution)"],"correct":2,"explanation":"الفوائد الثلاث المذكورة في سلايد 42 هي: إعادة استخدام الكود (Code reusability)، وأمان الأنواع (Type safety)، والأداء العالي وقت الترجمة (Performance). خيار C لا علاقة له بالقوالب.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:15","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الرابع • سلايد 43","question":"Q15: How does a Template differ from Function Overloading when handling multiple types?","options":["A) Templates require writing separate code bodies for every data type.","B) Overloading avoids writing redundant code, whereas Templates duplicate code.","C) Templates allow writing a single generic function, whereas Overloading requires writing multiple function definitions.","D) Overloading executes at compile-time, while Templates execute at runtime."],"correct":2,"explanation":"سلايد 43 وضعت مقارنة توضح أن الـ Template يسمح بكتابة دالة عامة واحدة فقط، بينما الـ Overloading يضطر المبرمج لتكرار كتابة الدالة لكل نوع بيانات.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-1.html:16","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Arrays & Templates","topic":"الجزء الرابع • سلايد 42","question":"Q16: What keyword in C++ is used to introduce a template definition?","options":["A) generic","B) virtual","C) template","D) typedef"],"correct":2,"explanation":"تبدأ صياغة القوالب دائماً بالكلمة المحجوزة template متبوعة بـ <typename T> أو <class T>.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-1.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:1","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الأول • سلايد 5","question":"Q1: What is the primary role of the \"Base Case\" in a recursive function?","options":["A) To allocate additional heap memory for recursive calls.","B) To provide a direct solution and terminate the recursion.","C) To execute the largest subproblem iteratively.","D) To call the main function once execution completes."],"correct":1,"explanation":"وظيفة الـ Base Case الأساسية هي توفير الحل المباشر لأبسط صورة وإيقاف استدعاء الدالة لنفسها (Stops recursion) حتى لا يستمر البرنامج للأبد.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:2","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الأول • سلايد 9","question":"Q2: What is a recursive function called when the LAST statement executed is the recursive call?","options":["A) Indirect Recursion","B) Infinite Recursion","C) Tail Recursion","D) Base Recursion"],"correct":2,"explanation":"التعريف النصي في سلايد 9: الدالة التي يكون آخر أمر تنفيذي فيها هو استدعاء نفسها تسمى Tail Recursive Function.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:3","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الأول • سلايد 10","question":"Q3: What causes an \"Infinite Recursion\" error during program runtime?","options":["A) Using too many for loops inside the recursive function.","B) Absence of a base case, or recursive steps that never reach the base case.","C) Passing pointers by value instead of by reference.","D) Declaring the function return type as void."],"correct":1,"explanation":"الاستدعاء اللانهائي (Infinite Recursion) يحدث عندما ننسى الـ Base Case أو عندما لا تقترب الخطوات المتكررة منه أبداً، فيمتلئ الـ Call Stack وتنفد الذاكرة وينهار البرنامج.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:4","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الأول • سلايد 7 و 8","question":"Q4: In executing `fact(4)`, which function call returns a value FIRST?","options":["A) fact(4)","B) fact(1)","C) fact(0)","D) All calls return at the exact same time."],"correct":2,"explanation":"في تتبع الذاكرة (Call Stack)، الدالة fact(0) هي التي تصل إلى الـ Base Case أولاً وترجع بالرقم 1 فوراً، وبعدها تبدأ الدوال المتجمدة بحساب قيمها تباعاً.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:5","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الثاني • سلايد 15 و 16","question":"Q5: Why does the recursive Fibonacci function `rFibNum` require TWO base cases instead of just one?","options":["A) Because it stores numbers in an array of size 2.","B) Because calculating the n-th Fibonacci number depends on the previous TWO values.","C) To prevent the function from compiling as a tail recursion.","D) Because Fibonacci numbers cannot be negative."],"correct":1,"explanation":"دالة فيبوناتشي تحتاج إلى حالتي توقف (n == 1 و n == 2) لأن معادلة السلسلة تعتمد على حاصل جمع رقمين سابقين (n - 1 و n - 2)، فلا يمكن التوقف عند حد واحد فقط.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:6","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الثاني • سلايد 17","question":"Q6: What is the return value of calling `rFibNum(2, 3, 4)` as traced in Lecture 3?","options":["A) 5","B) 6","C) 8","D) 13"],"correct":2,"explanation":"السلسلة تبدأ بالرقم الأول 2 ثم الثاني 3؛ إذن الرقم الثالث هو 2 + 3 = 5، والرقم الرابع هو 3 + 5 = 8، وهذا هو الناتج الرسمي في سلايد 17.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:7","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الثاني • سلايد 17","question":"Q7: How many times is the base case reached in the execution of `rFibNum(2, 3, 4)`?","options":["A) 1 time","B) 2 times","C) 3 times","D) 4 times"],"correct":2,"explanation":"من واقع شجرة الاستدعاء الرسمية في سلايد 17، وصلنا للـ Base Case ثلاث مرات: مرتان لـ rFibNum(2, 3, 2) ومرة واحدة لـ rFibNum(2, 3, 1).","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:8","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الثاني • سلايد 13","question":"Q8: What is the general mathematical formula for the n-th Fibonacci number when n >= 3?","options":["A) a_n = a_{n-1} * a_{n-2}","B) a_n = a_{n-1} + a_{n-2}","C) a_n = 2 * a_{n-1}","D) a_n = a_{n-1} - a_{n-2}"],"correct":1,"explanation":"التعريف الرياضي الدقيق المذكور في سلايد 13 هو جمع الحدين السابقين مباشرة: a_n = a_{n-1} + a_{n-2}.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:9","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الثالث • سلايد 22","question":"Q9: What is the base case condition for finding the largest element in an array `largest(list, lowerIndex, upperIndex)`?","options":["A) lowerIndex == 0","B) upperIndex == 0","C) lowerIndex == upperIndex","D) list[lowerIndex] == NULL"],"correct":2,"explanation":"حالة التوقف تكون عندما يتساوى الفهرسان (lowerIndex == upperIndex)، مما يعني أن النطاق الفرعي أصبح يحتوي على عنصر واحد فقط فهو الأكبر تلقائياً.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:10","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الثالث • سلايد 26 و 27","question":"Q10: How does `reversePrint` print a singly linked list in reverse order without using backward pointers?","options":["A) By converting the linked list into an array first.","B) By utilizing the system call stack to delay printing each node until all subsequent nodes have been processed.","C) By swapping the data fields of nodes iteratively.","D) By moving the head pointer to the tail node."],"correct":1,"explanation":"الدالة تستفيد من مكدس الاستدعاءات (System Call Stack)؛ حيث تؤجل طباعة العقدة الحالية وتستدعي العقدة التالية أولاً، وعند ارتداد الاستدعاءات من النهاية تُطبع العقد بالعكس.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:11","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الثالث • سلايد 24","question":"Q11: In the execution of `largest(list, 0, 3)` on `{23, 43, 35, 20}`, what value is returned by the base case call `largest(list, 3, 3)`?","options":["A) 43","B) 35","C) 20","D) 23"],"correct":2,"explanation":"الاستدعاء largest(list, 3, 3) يمثل الـ Base Case ويرجع بقيمة العنصر الموجود عند الفهرس 3 مباشرة وهو الرقم 20.","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"},{"id":"study/ds/lecture-3.html:12","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Recursion","topic":"الجزء الثالث • سلايد 27","question":"Q12: What would happen if we swapped the two statements in `reversePrint` so that `cout << current->data << \" \";` appears BEFORE `reversePrint(current->next);`?","options":["A) The list would be printed in normal forward order.","B) An infinite recursion error would occur.","C) A compilation syntax error would be generated.","D) Only the last node would be printed."],"correct":0,"explanation":"لو قمنا بالطباعة قبل الاستدعاء الذاتي، فستُطبع كل عقدة فور زيارتها، مما يطبع عناصر القائمة بالترتيب الطبيعي للأمام (Forward order).","sourceUrl":"study/ds/lecture-3.html"}],"computer-architecture":[{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:1","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Which of the following external devices is classified as \"Human-Readable\"?","options":["A) Magnetic tape drive","B) Video Display Terminal (VDT / Monitor)","C) Network Interface Card (NIC)","D) Temperature sensor"],"correct":1,"explanation":"أجهزة الـ Human-Readable هي الأجهزة المصممة للتواصل المباشر مع المستخدم البشري (إدخال بيانات بيده كالكيبورد، أو إخراج بيانات لعينه كالشاشة والبرنتر). أما الهارد والأشرطة والسنسورات فبتكلم ماكينات تانية (Machine-Readable)، وكارت الشبكة بيتواصل مع أجهزة بعيدة عبر خطوط نقل (Communication).","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:2","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Sensors, actuators, and magnetic disks are categorized under which peripheral classification?","options":["A) Human-readable devices","B) Communication devices","C) Machine-readable devices","D) Direct-bus devices"],"correct":2,"explanation":"الأجهزة دي مصممة للتعامل وتبادل البيانات مع أجهزة ومعدات الكمبيوتر الأخرى بدون تدخل بشري في قراءة الإشارة الخام؛ الحساس بيقيس حرارة ويبعتها ديجيتال، والمحرك بيستقبل نبضة كهربائية للتشغيل، والهارد بيخزن كتل ثنائية.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:3","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"How many unique characters can be represented using the standard International Reference Alphabet (IRA)?","options":["A) 64","B) 128","C) 256","D) 512"],"correct":1,"explanation":"نظام الـ IRA (وهو المعيار الدولي المكافئ لـ ASCII) بيعتمد فيزيائياً على كود ثنائي طوله 7-bit، وعدد الحالات أو الرموز المختلفة التي يمكن تمثيلها بـ 7 بت هو: 2^7 = 128 Characters.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:4","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"In the International Reference Alphabet (IRA), characters like Carriage Return and Line Feed are classified as:","options":["A) Printable characters","B) Control characters","C) Arithmetic characters","D) Parity characters"],"correct":1,"explanation":"رموز الـ IRA مقسومة نوعين: حروف وأرقام بتترسم على الشاشة أو الورق وتُقرأ بالعين (Printable)، ورموز تانية ملهاش شكل مطبوع ولكن وظيفتها إعطاء أوامر تحكم للشاشة أو الطابعة لتنظيم السطور وبداياتها (Control characters).","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:5","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Why is it practically impossible to connect peripheral devices directly to the system bus without an I/O module?","options":["A) Because peripherals operate with the exact same data formats as the CPU","B) Due to huge speed disparities, differing electrical/mechanical signals, and varying word lengths","C) Because the system bus only supports serial communication","D) Because external devices do not require power supplies"],"correct":1,"explanation":"المعالج إلكتروني فائق السرعة شغال بالجيجاهرتز وينقل 64 بت على التوازي، بينما الأجهزة الخارجية فيها أجزاء ميكانيكية بطيئة جداً، وبتستخدم إشارات مختلفة، وبتنقل تيار سيريال حرف بحرف. لو وصلناهم بالباص مباشرة المعالج هيتشل وهيتعطل.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:6","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Which major function of an I/O module prevents a fast processor from being held idle by a slow peripheral?","options":["A) Address recognition","B) Error detection","C) Data buffering","D) Bus arbitration"],"correct":2,"explanation":"وظيفة التخزين المؤقت (Data Buffering) معناها إن موديول الـ I/O فيه مسجلات داخلية (Buffers) بتستقبل كتلة البيانات من المعالج بسرعة البرق، والمعالج يمشي يشوف شغله، والموديول يفرغ الداتا دي براحته وبالسرعة البطيئة للجهاز الخارجي، والعكس عند الإدخال.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:7","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"When an I/O module decodes commands (READ, WRITE, STATUS) sent by the CPU, it is performing:","options":["A) Device communication","B) Processor communication","C) Error detection","D) Memory refreshing"],"correct":1,"explanation":"أي تعامل طرفاه هما 'المعالج' و'موديول الـ I/O' (زي فك شفرة أمر المعالج، إبلاغ المعالج بحالة الجهاز Ready/Busy، والتعرف على العنوان المطلوب) يندرج تحت وظيفة مخاطبة المعالج (Processor Communication).","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:8","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Detecting transmission bit errors (via parity) and mechanical faults (like a paper jam) is part of which I/O module function?","options":["A) Control and timing","B) Data buffering","C) Error detection","D) Address recognition"],"correct":2,"explanation":"موديول الـ I/O مسؤول عن مراقبة صحة وصول البيانات وخلوها من أخطاء النقل الكهربائي، بجانب استشعار أي عطل ميكانيكي هاردوير في الجهاز وإرسال تقرير خطأ فوري للمعالج.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:9","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"In Programmed I/O, how does the CPU determine whether the I/O device is ready for data transfer?","options":["A) It receives a hardware interrupt signal from the device","B) It continually tests the status register of the I/O module in a loop (busy-waiting / polling)","C) The DMA controller notifies the CPU via memory flags","D) The system clock forces the CPU to wait a fixed number of cycles"],"correct":1,"explanation":"في الـ Programmed I/O المعالج بيفضل محبوس ومقيد داخل حلقة تكرارية برمجية (Loop) مبيعملش أي حاجة في حياته غير إنه يقرا مسجل الحالة ويسأل: 'خلصت ولا لسه؟'، وده تعريف الـ Busy-Waiting / Polling اللي بيهدر وقت المعالج.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:10","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"What is the primary operational advantage of Interrupt-Driven I/O over Programmed I/O?","options":["A) It transfers data without passing through any processor registers","B) It frees the processor from busy-waiting, allowing it to execute other programs","C) It eliminates the need for an address bus","D) It guarantees higher data transfer speeds than DMA"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الميزة الحتمية اللي خلتنا نبتكر الـ Interrupt هي تحرير المعالج؛ المعالج بيصدر أمر القراءة للجهاز ويكمل تشغيل برامج تانية في الرامة، والجهاز أول ما يخلص هو اللي بيبعت إشارة سلكية (Interrupt) يرن على المعالج.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:11","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Why is Interrupt-Driven I/O still inefficient when transferring large blocks of data (e.g., from a hard drive)?","options":["A) Because peripherals cannot issue more than one interrupt per hour","B) Because the processor must still execute instructions to transfer each individual word between the I/O module and memory","C) Because interrupts permanently disable the processor's ALU","D) Because it requires analog cables"],"correct":1,"explanation":"عيب الـ Interrupt إنه بيقاطع المعالج مع كل كلمة واحدة (Word)، والمعالج بنفسه هو اللي بينقلها من مسجل الـ I/O للرامة. فلو بننقل ملف 100 ميجابايت، المعالج هيتقاطع ملايين المرات وهيضيع كل وقته في خدمة مقاطعات روتينية.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:12","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Which I/O technique enables the transfer of large blocks of data directly between an I/O module and main memory without continuous CPU intervention?","options":["A) Programmed I/O","B) Interrupt-Driven I/O","C) Direct Memory Access (DMA)","D) Software Polling"],"correct":2,"explanation":"الـ DMA هو الحل المعماري لنقل الكتل الكبيرة؛ بنجيب شريحة تحكم مستقلة (DMA Controller) هي اللي تمسك الباص وتنقل كتلة البيانات كاملة من الجهاز للذاكرة مباشرة دون أن يلمس المعالج أي بايت فيها.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:13","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"During a DMA operation, at what point does the DMA controller issue an interrupt to the processor?","options":["A) After every single byte transferred","B) Continuously throughout the transfer","C) Only once, after the entire block of data has been completely transferred","D) It never issues any interrupts to the processor"],"correct":2,"explanation":"المعالج بيدي أمر البداية للـ DMA وينساه تماماً. ولما الـ DMA يخلص نقل الـ 4096 بايت مثلاً للرامة، يبعت إشارة مقاطعة واحدة بس للمعالج في النهاية يقول له: 'تم نقل البلوك بنجاح'.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:14","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"In Memory-Mapped I/O, how are I/O ports addressed and accessed by the processor?","options":["A) Using dedicated I/O instructions like IN and OUT only","B) As part of a single shared address space, using standard memory instructions like LOAD and STORE","C) Through a separate bus completely isolated from memory","D) Using interrupt vector tables exclusively"],"correct":1,"explanation":"في الـ Memory-Mapped منافذ الأجهزة بتتعامل كأنها خلايا ذاكرة عادية في نفس الشارع وفضاء العناوين المشترك، وبالتالي نفس تعليمات قراءة وكتابة الذاكرة (LOAD/STORE) بتستخدم لقراءة وكتابة منافذ الأجهزة.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:15","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"What is the primary architectural penalty of choosing Memory-Mapped I/O over Isolated I/O?","options":["A) It requires complex extra control lines on the bus","B) It consumes part of the memory address space, reducing available memory capacity","C) It is completely incompatible with DMA","D) It slows down CPU register operations"],"correct":1,"explanation":"بما إن فضاء العناوين واحد مشترك؛ فلو المعالج مداه يعنون 4 جيجابايت، والعناوين من أول 0xF000 اتحجزت لمنافذ الشاشة والشبكة، العناوين دي متقدرش تركب مكانها رامات حقيقية، فبتاكل من سعة الذاكرة القصوى.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:16","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Isolated I/O (Port-Mapped I/O) differs from Memory-Mapped I/O because it features:","options":["A) A single shared address space for ports and RAM","B) Separate, independent address spaces for memory and I/O, requiring dedicated instructions like IN and OUT","C) No need for an address bus","D) Complete elimination of read/write control lines"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الـ Isolated بيفصل فضاء منافذ الأجهزة تماماً عن فضاء الذاكرة؛ وعشان نوصل لمنافذ الأجهزة كان لازم نخترع تعليمات خاصة في المعالج هي IN لقراءة المنفذ و OUT للكتابة فيه.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:17","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"In an Isolated I/O architecture, how does the hardware distinguish whether an address on the bus is meant for RAM or an I/O device?","options":["A) By measuring the physical resistance of the wires","B) By using distinct control lines (e.g., asserting Memory Read vs I/O Read)","C) By checking if the data is IRA text or binary numbers","D) By running a software polling loop"],"correct":1,"explanation":"لأن العنوان ممكن يتطابق (مثلاً العنوان 10 موجود في الرام وموجود في المنافذ)، فالمعالج لازم ينور سلك تحكم إضافي على الباص: لو فعل إشارة Memory Read الرامة تستجيب، ولو فعل إشارة I/O Read موديول الجهاز هو اللي يرد.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:18","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Which technique for identifying an interrupting device uses a dedicated physical wire from each peripheral to the CPU?","options":["A) Daisy chaining","B) Software polling","C) Multiple interrupt lines","D) Bus arbitration"],"correct":2,"explanation":"الطريقة دي بتخصص خط كهربائي مستقل لكل جهاز يوصل برجل مخصوصة في المعالج، فالمعالج يعرف صاحب المقاطعة فوراً من السلكة اللي ارتفع فيها الجهد.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:19","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"What is the main drawback of the \"Multiple Interrupt Lines\" scheme?","options":["A) It is the slowest scheme available","B) It is severely constrained by the limited number of physical pins on the processor chip","C) It requires the CPU to execute a polling program","D) It cannot work with keyboard devices"],"correct":1,"explanation":"المعالج شريحة مدمجة صغيرة وعدد أرجله (Pins) محدود جداً؛ مستحيل عملياً نخصص 40 أو 50 رجل لمقاطعات أجهزة خارجية ونسيب باقي الوظائف الحيوية.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:20","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"In the Software Poll method for identifying an interrupt, what action does the CPU take?","options":["A) It sends an acknowledgement signal along a serial hardware chain","B) It executes a service routine that sequentially tests each device's status register until the requester is found","C) It commands the DMA controller to take over the identification","D) It forces all devices to reset simultaneously"],"correct":1,"explanation":"أول ما المقاطعة العامة توصل، المعالج بيشغل برنامج بيلف على الأجهزة واحد ورا التاني بالترتيب يقرا مسجل الحالة بتاعهم: 'أنت اللي طلبت مقاطعة؟'، لحد ما يلاقي الجهاز المطلوب. عيبها إنها بطيئة برمجياً.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:21","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"In a Daisy Chain (Hardware Poll) configuration, how is the device priority physically determined?","options":["A) Alphabetically by device name","B) By the device's physical position along the Interrupt Acknowledge (INTA) line","C) By the speed of the device's internal buffer","D) Dynamically by the operating system scheduler"],"correct":1,"explanation":"إشارة الموافقة على المقاطعة (INTA) بتمر متسلسلة من جهاز للتاني؛ الجهاز المتوصل في أول السلك (الأقرب للمعالج) بيشوف الإشارة الأول، فلو كان طالب مقاطعة بياخدها ويمنعها عن الباقيين، وبالتالي أولوية الجهاز محددة بمكانه الفيزيائي في السلسلة.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:22","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"What does an I/O module place on the data bus when it is acknowledged in a Vectored Interrupt scheme (like Daisy Chain)?","options":["A) The entire data file","B) An Interrupt Vector (identifying code / pointer to its ISR)","C) Its clock frequency","D) The IRA parity table"],"correct":1,"explanation":"في أنظمة الـ Vectored الجهاز الفائز مش بيبعت الداتا فوراً؛ بيبعت كود تعريفي اسمه Interrupt Vector، المعالج بيستخدمه كمؤشر لعنوان دالة الخدمة الخاصة بالجهاز ده في جدول المقاطعات عشان يشغل البرنامج الصح مباشرة.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:23","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"In Bus Arbitration for interrupt handling, what must a device achieve before asserting its interrupt request?","options":["A) It must switch from Programmed I/O to DMA mode","B) It must request and win master control of the system bus from a bus arbiter","C) It must empty all memory cache lines","D) It must format its data according to IRA standards"],"correct":1,"explanation":"خطوط الباص وسيلة مشتركة ونادرة؛ في نظام الـ Bus Arbitration الجهاز ملوش حق يبعت مقاطعة ولا يرمي الـ Vector بتاعه إلا لما يقدم طلب لوحدة تحكيم الباص (Bus Arbiter) وتمنحه حق السيطرة كـ Bus Master.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:24","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Which I/O command type is used to check various status conditions (e.g., error bits, busy/ready) associated with an I/O module?","options":["A) Control command","B) Test command","C) Read command","D) Write command"],"correct":1,"explanation":"موديول الـ I/O بيستقبل 4 أوامر رئيسية من المعالج: 1. Control: لتشغيل الطرفية وتوجيهها. 2. Test: لاختبار وفحص شروط الحالة (Status conditions) والتأكد إن الجهاز متاح وخالي من الأخطاء. 3. Read: لجلب البيانات من الجهاز للبافر. 4. Write: لإرسال البيانات من الباص للجهاز.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"},{"id":"study/arch/chapter-7.html:25","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","topic":"المحاضرة 5: Input / Output & DMA","question":"Which of the following summaries correctly matches each I/O technique with its primary CPU involvement?","options":["A) Programmed I/O: Zero CPU involvement | DMA: Busy-waiting CPU","B) Programmed I/O: Busy-waiting CPU | Interrupt-Driven: CPU handles word transfers | DMA: CPU handles only block setup and completion","C) Interrupt-Driven: Transfers blocks directly to RAM | DMA: Handles single characters","D) Programmed I/O: Uses dedicated DMA chips | Isolated I/O: Uses shared memory spaces"],"correct":1,"explanation":"دي خلاصة الفصل كله: Programmed: المعالج محبوس يراقب ويفحص (Busy-waiting). Interrupt-Driven: المعالج حر لكن بيتدخل لنقل كل كلمة ورا كلمة عند المقاطعة. DMA: المعالج بيسلم أمر البداية ويستقبل إشعار النهاية، ونقل البلوك كله بيتم مباشرة بين الجهاز والرامة.","sourceUrl":"study/arch/chapter-7.html"}],"database-systems":[{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:1","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 1: المفاهيم الأساسية","question":"A collection of known facts that can be recorded and have an implicit meaning is formally defined as:","options":["Database","Program","Data","Schema"],"correct":2,"explanation":"التعريف الحرفي في السلايد: Known facts that can be recorded and have an implicit meaning هو تعريف الـ Data.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:2","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 1: المفاهيم الأساسية","question":"The specific part of the real world that a database represents and stores data about is known as:","options":["Operating System","Data Dictionary","Universe of Discourse (UoD)","Database State"],"correct":2,"explanation":"جزء الواقع الذي تمثله قاعدة البيانات يسمى Mini-World أو الاسم العلمي المكافئ له Universe of Discourse (UoD).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:3","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 1: المفاهيم الأساسية","question":"Which of the following is NOT a required property of a database according to the textbook definition?","options":["It is a logically coherent collection of data with inherent meaning.","It represents some aspect of the real world.","It must store only numeric and textual data.","It is designed, built, and populated for a specific purpose."],"correct":2,"explanation":"قواعد البيانات لا تقتصر على الأرقام والنصوص فقط، بل تشمل أيضاً الصور والفيديو والخرائط والجينات في التطبيقات الحديثة.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:4","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 1: المفاهيم الأساسية","question":"When an event occurs in the mini-world (e.g., a student registers for a course), what must happen to maintain data integrity?","options":["The database schema must be recreated.","The change must be reflected in the database.","A new DBMS must be installed.","All application programs must be recompiled."],"correct":1,"explanation":"أي تغيير يحدث في العالم المصغر (Mini-world) يجب أن ينعكس فوراً في قاعدة البيانات (Reflected in the database).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:5","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 2: وظائف وبيئة الـ DBMS","question":"A general-purpose software system that facilitates the processes of defining, constructing, manipulating, and sharing databases is called:","options":["Operating System","DBMS","Application Program","Database Schema"],"correct":1,"explanation":"نظام إدارة قواعد البيانات (DBMS) هو النظام البرمجي العام المسؤول عن الوظائف الأربعة: Defining, Constructing, Manipulating, Sharing.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:6","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 2: وظائف وبيئة الـ DBMS","question":"Specifying the structures, data types, and constraints for the data to be stored is the definition of which DBMS functionality?","options":["Constructing","Sharing","Defining","Manipulating"],"correct":2,"explanation":"تحديد الهياكل وأنواع البيانات والقيود (Constraints) هو تعريف وظيفة الـ Defining.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:7","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 2: وظائف وبيئة الـ DBMS","question":"Storing the data on a physical storage medium controlled by the DBMS is referred to as:","options":["Defining","Constructing","Manipulating","Querying"],"correct":1,"explanation":"عملية تخزين البيانات فعلياً على وسيط تخزين (الهارد ديسك) تحت سيطرة الـ DBMS تسمى Constructing.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:8","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 2: وظائف وبيئة الـ DBMS","question":"An application that retrieves specific records and formats them into a printable document is executing which DBMS function?","options":["Defining","Constructing","Manipulating","Sharing"],"correct":2,"explanation":"الاستعلام (Querying) والتحديث واستخراج التقارير المطبوعة كلها تندرج تحت وظيفة Manipulating.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:9","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 2: وظائف وبيئة الـ DBMS","question":"Protection of the database against power failures or disk crashes is specifically classified as:","options":["Security Protection","Concurrency Protection","System Protection","Logical Protection"],"correct":2,"explanation":"الحماية ضد أعطال الهاردوير أو انقطاع الكهرباء تسمى System Protection، بينما الحماية ضد الاختراق تسمى Security Protection.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:10","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 2: وظائف وبيئة الـ DBMS","question":"Which of the following is considered one of the internal software modules of a DBMS in a simplified database system environment?","options":["Application Programs","Database Users","Software to process queries/programs","Operating system compiler"],"correct":2,"explanation":"داخل صندوق الـ DBMS Software يوجد جزآن داخليان: Software to process queries/programs و Software to access stored data.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:11","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 2: الـ Meta-data والكتالوج","question":"Data that describes the structure, types, and constraints of the primary database is formally known as:","options":["Transaction data","Meta-data","View data","Application data"],"correct":1,"explanation":"البيانات التي تصف هيكل وأنواع وشروط قاعدة البيانات (Data about data) تسمى Meta-data.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:12","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 2: الـ Meta-data والكتالوج","question":"In a DBMS, where is the meta-data stored and maintained?","options":["Hardcoded inside each application program","In the operating system registry","In the DBMS catalog (data dictionary)","In user session cookies"],"correct":2,"explanation":"يتم حفظ الـ Meta-data في كتالوج مركزي مستقل داخل الـ DBMS يسمى DBMS Catalog أو Data Dictionary.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:13","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 2: الـ Meta-data والكتالوج","question":"The capability of a database system to contain both the data and the complete definition of its structure is referred to as:","options":["Program-Data Independence","Concurrency Control","Self-describing nature of a database","Data Redundancy"],"correct":2,"explanation":"احتواء النظام على البيانات مع وصفها الكامل في الكتالوج يعرف بخاصية الوصف الذاتي (Self-describing nature).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:14","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 2: الـ Meta-data والكتالوج","question":"In a simplified database catalog, the description of column names, data types, and their belonging tables represents:","options":["Application code","Meta-data","End-user queries","Backup log files"],"correct":1,"explanation":"تفاصيل أسماء الأعمدة وأنواعها والجداول التابعة لها داخل الكتالوج هي أمثلة مباشرة على الـ Meta-data.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:15","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 3: أنواع وتطبيقات قواعد البيانات","question":"Databases that specifically store and analyze maps, satellite images, and weather patterns are known as:","options":["Multimedia Databases","Geographic Information Systems (GIS)","Genome Databases","Traditional Textual Databases"],"correct":1,"explanation":"تخزين وتحليل الخرائط وصور الأقمار الصناعية وبيانات الطقس هو تخصص نظم المعلومات الجغرافية (GIS).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:16","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 3: أنواع وتطبيقات قواعد البيانات","question":"Storing DNA sequences and molecular structures is an example of which modern database application?","options":["Biological and Genome Databases","Data Warehousing","Traditional Databases","Real-time ERP Systems"],"correct":0,"explanation":"سلاسل الـ DNA والشفرات الجينية يتم تخزينها في قواعد البيانات الحيوية والجينية (Biological and Genome Databases).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:17","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 3: أنواع وتطبيقات قواعد البيانات","question":"Which of the following is considered a Traditional database application?","options":["Social network graph analysis","Geographic Information System (GIS)","Numeric and textual accounting database","Multimedia video streaming database"],"correct":2,"explanation":"التطبيقات التقليدية (Traditional Applications) هي قواعد البيانات الرقمية والنصية (Numeric and textual).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:18","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 3: أنواع وتطبيقات قواعد البيانات","question":"Systems used to aggregate data from multiple massive sources to assist executives in decision making and Business Intelligence (BI) are called:","options":["Real-time operating systems","Data Warehouses","Transaction logs","Traditional file directories"],"correct":1,"explanation":"مستودعات البيانات (Data Warehouses) تجمع البيانات الضخمة لدعم اتخاذ القرارات والـ Business Intelligence (BI).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:19","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 3: أنواع وتطبيقات قواعد البيانات","question":"Search engines that index massive amounts of textual and multimedia data from the World Wide Web are classified under:","options":["Traditional Numeric Applications","Recent Developments in Database Applications","File Processing Systems","Standalone Local Utilities"],"correct":1,"explanation":"محركات البحث (Search Engines) والحوسبة السحابية تندرج تحت التطورات الحديثة (Recent Developments in Database Applications).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:20","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 4: الخصائص الأربعة لمدخل الداتابيز","question":"The characteristic that allows modifying the data storage structures without having to modify the application programs is known as:","options":["Data Abstraction","Program-Data Independence","Concurrency Control","Atomicity"],"correct":1,"explanation":"القدرة على تعديل هيكل تخزين البيانات دون الحاجة لتعديل كود البرامج هي استقلالية البرامج عن البيانات (Program-Data Independence).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:21","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 4: الخصائص الأربعة لمدخل الداتابيز","question":"A DBMS feature that presents a subset of the database or dynamically computed virtual data to a specific group of users is called a:","options":["Catalog","View","Transaction","Schema construct"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الـ View تعرض جزءاً مخصصاً من الداتابيز أو بيانات افتراضية محسوبة (Virtual derived data) مثل الـ GPA.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:22","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 4: الخصائص الأربعة لمدخل الداتابيز","question":"Which software module within the DBMS ensures that simultaneous data modifications by multiple users do not result in corrupted or inconsistent data?","options":["Concurrency Control Software","Operating System Scheduler","Data Dictionary","Application Compiler"],"correct":0,"explanation":"برمجيات التحكم في التزامن (Concurrency Control Software) تضمن عدم تضارب تعديلات المستخدمين المتزامنة.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:23","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 4: الخصائص الأربعة لمدخل الداتابيز","question":"The transaction property which guarantees that either ALL operations of a transaction are executed successfully or NONE are applied is called:","options":["Isolation","Consistency","Durability","Atomicity"],"correct":3,"explanation":"خاصية الذرية (Atomicity - الكل أو لا شيء) تضمن تنفيذ كل خطوات المعاملة بالكامل أو إلغائها بالكامل.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:24","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 4: الخصائص الأربعة لمدخل الداتابيز","question":"The conceptual representation of data that hides storage details and supports program-data independence is achieved through:","options":["Data Redundancy","Data Abstraction","Operating system directories","Hardcoded file routines"],"correct":1,"explanation":"تجريد البيانات (Data Abstraction) هو الذي يخفي تفاصيل التخزين المعقدة ويحقق استقلالية البرامج عن البيانات.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:25","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 5: مستخدمو قواعد البيانات","question":"A bank teller who continuously processes customer deposits and withdrawals using pre-programmed standard interfaces is classified as a:","options":["Casual End User","Parametric / Naive End User","Sophisticated End User","Database Administrator"],"correct":1,"explanation":"موظف البنك أو الحجز الذي يستخدم شاشات جاهزة ومعاملات مسبقة البرمجة (Canned transactions) يصنف كـ Parametric / Naive End User.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:26","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 5: مستخدمو قواعد البيانات","question":"Who among the following is primarily responsible for authorizing access, acquiring software/hardware resources, and monitoring system performance?","options":["Database Designer","Application Programmer","Database Administrator (DBA)","Tool Developer"],"correct":2,"explanation":"مدير قاعدة البيانات (DBA) هو المسؤول عن منح الصلاحيات، توفير الموارد، ومراقبة الأداء والأمان.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:27","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 5: مستخدمو قواعد البيانات","question":"Which user group interacts with the database only occasionally and requires different, customized information each time (such as middle and high-level managers)?","options":["Casual End Users","Parametric Users","Standalone Users","DBMS Implementers"],"correct":0,"explanation":"المستخدم العارض (Casual End User) كالمديرين يدخل على فترات متباعدة ويطلب معلومات مختلفة في كل مرة.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:28","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 5: مستخدمو قواعد البيانات","question":"Which of the following database users is classified as an \"Actor BEHIND the Scene\"?","options":["Database Administrator (DBA)","Database Designer","DBMS Tool Developer","System Analyst"],"correct":2,"explanation":"مطورو الأدوات (DBMS Tool Developers) ومصممو محرك الـ DBMS ومشغلو الأجهزة هم أبطال خلف الكواليس (Behind the Scene).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:29","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 5: مستخدمو قواعد البيانات","question":"Pre-written and thoroughly tested standard queries and updates used by parametric users are officially called:","options":["Dynamic scripts","Canned transactions","Physical indexes","Metadata logs"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الاستعلامات والتحديثات الجاهزة والمبرمجة مسبقاً للمستخدم النمطي تسمى رسمياً Canned transactions.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:30","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 6: مميزات الـ DBMS ومتى نتجنبه","question":"In traditional file systems, data duplication across multiple departments often leads to:","options":["Data Independence","Data Inconsistency","Better security","Faster indexing"],"correct":1,"explanation":"تكرار البيانات غير المتحكم فيه في أنظمة الملفات القديمة يؤدي إلى تناقض البيانات (Data Inconsistency) وإهدار المساحة.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:31","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 6: مميزات الـ DBMS ومتى نتجنبه","question":"Auxiliary storage structures such as indexes are provided by a DBMS primarily to:","options":["Enforce security permissions","Speed up query retrieval performance","Translate high-level DDL into machine code","Duplicate data for backup purposes"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الفهارس (Indexes) هي هياكل تخزين مساعدة وظيفتها الأساسية تسريع البحث واسترجاع الاستعلامات.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:32","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 6: مميزات الـ DBMS ومتى نتجنبه","question":"Rules specified in active databases that trigger automated actions when certain events take place are called:","options":["Canned transactions","Triggers","Indexes","Views"],"correct":1,"explanation":"القواعد التي تطلق إجراءات تلقائية عند وقوع حدث معين في قواعد البيانات النشطة تسمى Triggers.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:33","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 6: مميزات الـ DBMS ومتى نتجنبه","question":"In which of the following scenarios is using a full-scale DBMS NOT recommended?","options":["A multi-branch commercial banking system","A university registration portal with thousands of concurrent students","A simple embedded controller with stringent real-time response requirements","An e-commerce platform with dynamic inventory updates"],"correct":2,"explanation":"الأنظمة المدمجة البسيطة التي تتطلب استجابة لحظية حرجة (Stringent real-time requirements) لا ينصح فيها باستخدام DBMS بسبب الـ Overhead.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-1.html:34","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Databases and Database Users","topic":"البلوك 6: مميزات الـ DBMS ومتى نتجنبه","question":"The financial and operational advantage of consolidating the data processing requirements of an entire enterprise into a single DBMS is referred to as:","options":["Program-data independence","Economies of scale","Data abstraction","Controlled isolation"],"correct":1,"explanation":"دمج متطلبات المؤسسة كلها في نظام واحد لتوفير التكلفة والموارد يعرف اقتصادياً بـ Economies of scale.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-1.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:1","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"نماذج البيانات وتجريد البيانات","question":"The suppression of details of data organization and storage and the highlighting of essential features is formally defined as:","options":["Database Instance","Data Abstraction","Data Model Construct","Schema Evolution"],"correct":1,"explanation":"التعريف الحرفي في سلايد 3: تجريد البيانات (Data Abstraction) هو إخفاء التفاصيل التخزينية وإبراز الخصائص الجوهرية لفهم أفضل.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:2","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"نماذج البيانات وتجريد البيانات","question":"Which component of a data model specifies the dynamic aspect or behavior of a database application (e.g., COMPUTE_GPA)?","options":["Data types","Constraints","Basic operations","Internal mappings"],"correct":2,"explanation":"سلايد 4: العمليات الأساسية (Basic operations) هي التي تحدد الجانب الديناميكي أو السلوك لقاعدة البيانات مثل استدعاء دالة COMPUTE_GPA.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:3","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"نماذج البيانات وتجريد البيانات","question":"Conceptual (high-level) data models provide concepts that are:","options":["Close to the hardware registers and magnetic tracks","Close to the way many users perceive data","Dependent on the physical network protocol","Only understandable by the database kernel"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 5 و 6: النماذج المفاهيمية (Conceptual models) تقدم مفاهيم قريبة جداً من طريقة إدراك وفهم البشر للبيانات في العالم الحقيقي.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:4","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"نماذج البيانات وتجريد البيانات","question":"The three core concepts provided by conceptual data models (such as the ER model) are:","options":["Bytes, Sectors, and Tracks","Entities, Attributes, and Relationships","Tables, Primary Keys, and Foreign Keys","Procedures, Triggers, and Cursors"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 6: المفاهيم الثلاثة المكونة للنموذج المفاهيمي هي: الكيان (Entity)، الخاصية (Attribute)، والعلاقة (Relationship).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:5","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"نماذج البيانات وتجريد البيانات","question":"The Relational Data Model is classified under which category of data models?","options":["Physical data models","Conceptual data models","Representational (Implementation) data models","Low-level models"],"correct":2,"explanation":"سلايد 5 و 7: النموذج العلائقي (Relational model) يصنف ضمن النماذج التمثيلية / التطبيقية (Representational data models).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:6","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"نماذج البيانات وتجريد البيانات","question":"Because traditional commercial relational DBMSs represent data as record structures, they are also referred to as:","options":["Object-based data models","Record-based data models","Network-less models","Pointer-based models"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 7: النموذج العلائقي يمثل البيانات كهياكل سجلات، ولذلك يسمى أيضاً Record-based data models.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:7","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"نماذج البيانات وتجريد البيانات","question":"A structure that makes the search for particular database records efficient, such as an Index, is classified under which model category?","options":["Conceptual data models","Representational data models","Physical (low-level) data models","View models"],"correct":2,"explanation":"سلايد 5 و 9: مسارات الوصول (Access paths) والفهارس (Indexes) تقع ضمن النماذج الفيزيائية منخفضة المستوى (Physical data models).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:8","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"المخطط والحالة واللقطة","question":"The description of a database that is specified during database design and is NOT expected to change frequently is called the:","options":["Database State","Database Schema (Intension)","Database Snapshot","Database Instance"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 11: المخطط (Schema) أو الـ Intension هو وصف وتصميم قاعدة البيانات ويتغير نادراً جداً.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:9","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"المخطط والحالة واللقطة","question":"What does a \"Schema Diagram\" display?","options":["The actual data values of all rows","The structure of each record type, but NOT actual instances","The physical sector addresses on the disk","The history of all delete operations"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 11 و 12: رسمة المخطط (Schema Diagram) تعرض هيكل وسجلات الجداول فقط، ولا تعرض أي سجلات أو قيم فعلية إطلاقاً.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:10","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"المخطط والحالة واللقطة","question":"The actual data stored in a database at a particular moment in time is called the:","options":["Schema Diagram","Database Construct","Database State (Extension)","Data Abstraction"],"correct":2,"explanation":"سلايد 13: البيانات الفعلية المخزنة في لحظة زمنية معينة تسمى حالة قاعدة البيانات (Database State) أو Extension أو Snapshot.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:11","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"المخطط والحالة واللقطة","question":"Every time an insert, update, or delete operation is executed on the database, what happens?","options":["The database schema changes","The database transitions to another database state","The conceptual schema must be recompiled","The DDL statements are re-executed"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 13 و 15: مع كل عملية تعديل أو إضافة نحصل على حالة جديدة لقاعدة البيانات (another database state).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:12","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"المخطط والحالة واللقطة","question":"A database state that satisfies all the specified structure and constraints of the database is called a:","options":["Initial State","Valid State","Static State","Intension"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 13: الحالة الصالحة (Valid State) هي الحالة التي تحترم وتلبي جميع الشروط والقيود المعرفة لقاعدة البيانات.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:13","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"المستويات الثلاثة والاستقلالية","question":"What is the primary goal of the Three-Schema Architecture?","options":["To merge hardware and software into one layer","To separate the user applications from the physical database","To eliminate the need for SQL queries","To enforce centralization on a single computer"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 18: الهدف الأساسي لمعمارية المستويات الثلاثة هو فصل برامج وشاشات المستخدمين عن قاعدة البيانات الفيزيائية.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:14","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"المستويات الثلاثة والاستقلالية","question":"Which schema level describes the physical storage structure, file allocation, and access paths?","options":["External schema","Conceptual schema","Internal schema","View schema"],"correct":2,"explanation":"سلايد 18 و 20: المستوى الداخلي (Internal schema) هو الذي يصف البنية الفيزيائية للتخزين ومسارات الوصول.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:15","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"المستويات الثلاثة والاستقلالية","question":"Which schema level describes the structure of the entire database for a community of users while hiding physical storage details?","options":["Internal Level","Conceptual Level","External View","SDL Layer"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 18 و 20: المستوى المفاهيمي (Conceptual level) يصف هيكل قاعدة البيانات بالكامل ويخفي التفاصيل الفيزيائية.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:16","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"المستويات الثلاثة والاستقلالية","question":"The capacity to alter the conceptual schema without having to alter external schemas or application programs is called:","options":["Physical data independence","Logical data independence","Schema evolution","Program-storage independence"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 22: استقلالية البيانات المنطقية (Logical Data Independence) تعني تعديل الـ Conceptual Schema دون أن تتأثر شاشات المستخدمين.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:17","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"المستويات الثلاثة والاستقلالية","question":"The capacity to alter the internal schema (e.g., adding an index or moving disk files) without having to alter the conceptual schema is called:","options":["Logical data independence","Physical data independence","VDL Independence","Conceptual Evolution"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 22: استقلالية البيانات الفيزيائية (Physical Data Independence) تعني تعديل الـ Internal Schema دون تعديل الـ Conceptual Schema.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:18","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"معماريات السيرفرات والأنظمة","question":"In a Two-Tier Client/Server architecture, where do application programs typically run?","options":["On the Database Server","On the Client machine","On the Print Server","On the Storage Area Network"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 29: في معمارية الـ Two-Tier يعمل كود التطبيق وبرامج المستخدم على جهاز العميل (Client machine).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:19","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"معماريات السيرفرات والأنظمة","question":"In a Three-Tier Client/Server architecture, the intermediate layer (Application/Web server) is responsible for:","options":["Formatting magnetic disk sectors","Running application programs and storing business rules","Displaying the physical CRT monitor beam","Compiling database BIOS routines"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سلايد 30 و 31: السيرفر الوسيط (Application server) يشغل كود التطبيق ويخزن قواعد العمل (Business rules).","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"study/db/chapter-2.html:20","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Database Concepts & Architecture","topic":"معماريات السيرفرات والأنظمة","question":"Which DBMS language is specifically used to define user views and their mappings to the conceptual schema?","options":["DDL","SDL","VDL (View Definition Language)","DML"],"correct":2,"explanation":"سلايد 23: لغة الـ VDL (View Definition Language) مخصصة لتحديد واجهات ورؤى المستخدمين وربطها بالمستوى المفاهيمي.","sourceUrl":"study/db/chapter-2.html"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:1","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Database Types & Course Scope","question":"Which category of database applications does this academic course primarily focus on?","options":["Traditional applications (Numeric and Textual databases)","Biological and Genome Databases exclusively","Massive Video and Multimedia Streaming only","Advanced Real-time Geographic Information Systems (GIS)"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: السلايد 3 بتنص بوضوح تحت: 'Our course focuses on traditional applications'، يعني القواعد الرقمية والنصية التقليدية مش الجينوم ولا الوسائط الضخمة.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:2","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Recent Developments","question":"Why do search engines like Google, Bing, and Yahoo collect massive repositories of web pages?","options":["For searching and indexing purposes","To eliminate computer memory caches","To bypass database authentication protocols","To replace relational data models"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: محركات البحث بتجمع أرشيف وصفحات الويب عشان الفهرسة والبحث السريع (Searching and indexing purposes) لما المستخدم يبحث.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:3","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Basic Definitions - Data","question":"In database theory, 'Known facts that can be recorded and have an implicit meaning' is the exact definition of:","options":["Data","Information Systems","DBMS Engine","Computer Hardware"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: ده التعريف الحرفي والأكاديمي للـ Data في السلايد 5؛ حقائق نقدر نسجلها وليها معنى ضمني مفهوم.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:4","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Basic Definitions - Mini-world","question":"What technical term describes 'some part of the real world about which data is stored in a database'?","options":["Mini-world (Universe of Discourse - UoD)","Operating System Kernel","Network Protocol Buffer","Database Schema Catalog"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: الجزء من العالم الواقعي اللي بنخزن بياناته بنسميه Mini-world أو Universe of Discourse (UoD)، وزي ما قلنا أي تغيير فيه بينعكس في الداتا بيز.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:5","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Basic Definitions - DBMS","question":"A software package or system designed to facilitate the creation and maintenance of a computerized database is called:","options":["Database Management System (DBMS)","Spreadsheet Document Viewer","Central Processing Unit","Text Editor Application"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: السوفت وير اللي مسؤول عن إنشاء وصيانة قاعدة البيانات هو الـ DBMS (زي MySQL أو Oracle).","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:6","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Basic Definitions - Database System","question":"What constitutes a 'Database System' according to fundamental definitions?","options":["The DBMS software together with the data itself (and sometimes applications)","The computer power supply cable alone","An unformatted external storage tape","A printed user instruction manual"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: الـ Database System هو السوفت وير (DBMS) مضافاً إليه البيانات نفسها المتخزنة وتطبيقاتها.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:7","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Meta-data & Catalog","question":"Where is database descriptive information and definition (meta-data) stored by the DBMS?","options":["In the database catalog or dictionary","Hardcoded inside user application client source code","In temporary RAM buffer cache that erases on reboot","On external paper punch cards"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: الميتا-داتا (Meta-data) بتتخزن حصراً في الـ Database Catalog أو قاموس البيانات (Dictionary) الخاص بالـ DBMS.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:8","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Application Activities - Transactions","question":"Which database activity involves reading data, updating certain values, or generating and storing new data?","options":["Transactions","Static Read-Only Queries","Monitor Screen Calibration","Keyboard Character Scanning"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: الـ Transaction هي المعاملة اللي بتقرأ وتعدل (Update) قيم أو تولد داتا جديدة وتخزنها، مش مجرد استعلام قراءة عادي.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:9","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Additional Functionality - Protection","question":"Protecting the database system against hardware or software malfunction (or crashes) is classified as:","options":["System protection","Security protection against hackers","Screen graphic acceleration","Printer spooling management"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: الحماية ضد أعطال الهاردوير وانهيار البرمجيات (Crashes) اسمها في السلايد 9 'System protection'.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:10","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Architecture - Environment","question":"In the simplified database system environment diagram (Figure 1.1), which software module processes and compiles queries?","options":["Software to Process Queries/Programs","Hardware Bus Controller","Power Regulator Chip","Optical Drive Reader"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: أول مكون برمجي بيستقبل الاستعلامات ويفسرها في شكل 1.1 هو 'Software to Process Queries/Programs'.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:11","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Conceptual Modeling - ER Model","question":"Real-world entities and their relationships (like UNIVERSITY entities) are typically expressed in which conceptual model?","options":["ENTITY-RELATIONSHIP (ER) data model","Assembly 8086 Instruction Set","TCP/IP Networking Protocol Stack","Von Neumann Hardware Architecture"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: السلايد 12 بتأكد إن الكيانات والعلاقات بنعبر عنها بنموذج مفاهيمي شهير هو الـ Entity-Relationship (ER) model.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:12","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Core Characteristics - Data Independence","question":"What characteristic allows changing data structures and storage organization without changing access programs?","options":["Program-data independence","Network packet routing","Hard drive rotation latency","Screen aspect ratio scaling"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: ده التعريف الأهم في المحاضرة: استقلالية البرامج عن البيانات (Program-data independence) بتسمح بتعديل هياكل التخزين دون الحاجة لتعديل برامج الوصول.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:13","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Database Catalog Structure","question":"In the simplified catalog example (Figure 1.3), which table stores Column_name, Data_type, and Belongs_to_relation?","options":["COLUMNS","RELATIONS","GRADE_REPORT","STUDENT_ACCOUNTS"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: جدول COLUMNS في الكتالوج هو اللي متسجل فيه اسم كل عمود ونوع بياناته والجدول التابع ليه.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:14","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Program-Operation Independence","question":"In Program-operation independence, which part includes the operation name and the data types of its arguments?","options":["The Interface","The Implementation","The Physical Sector Track","The Optical Laser Lens"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: السلايد 16 وضحت إن الـ Interface بيشمل اسم العملية وأنواع الـ arguments، بينما الـ Implementation هو كود التنفيذ اللي نقدر نغيره براحتنا.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:15","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Multiple Views of Data","question":"Why does a modern DBMS provide support for multiple views of the data?","options":["To allow each user to see only the data of interest to that specific user","To duplicate disk storage needlessly across multiple servers","To restrict network bandwidth speed during peak hours","To force all developers to write machine language"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: السلايد 17 بينت إن الـ Multiple views بتخلي كل فئة من المستخدمين تشوف View خاصة بالبيانات اللي تهمها بس (Data of interest).","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:16","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Concurrency & Recovery Subsystem","question":"Which component inside the DBMS ensures that each completed transaction has its effect permanently recorded?","options":["Recovery subsystem","Keyboard interrupt buffer","Temporary clipboard stack","Screen display refresh controller"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: السلايد 18 حددت إن الـ 'Recovery subsystem' هو المسؤول عن ضمان بقاء وتسجيل أثر أي معاملة مكتملة بشكل دائم في قاعدة البيانات.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:17","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Database Users - DBA Role","question":"Who is primarily responsible for authorizing access, monitoring efficiency, and acquiring software/hardware resources?","options":["Database Administrator (DBA)","Application Programmer","Casual End User","Tool Developer"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: منح وتفويض الصلاحيات وتوفير الموارد ومراقبة كفاءة التشغيل دي وظيفة مدير قاعدة البيانات (DBA).","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:18","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Database Users - Naïve/Parametric","question":"Bank tellers and mobile app users who perform predefined 'canned transactions' belong to which category?","options":["Naïve or Parametric end users","Database Administrators (DBA)","System Implementors","Stand-alone Users"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: صرافو البنوك ومستخدمو الموبايل اللي بيتعاملوا مع معاملات جاهزة (canned transactions) هما Naïve or Parametric users.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:19","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Advantages - Normalization","question":"Storing each logical data item in only one place in the database to ensure consistency and save storage space is called:","options":["Data normalization","Data encryption scrambling","Memory stack swapping","Processor instruction caching"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: تخزين كل معلومة في مكان واحد فقط لمنع التكرار وضمان الاتساق هو تعريف الـ Data Normalization في السلايد 25.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2:20","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2","topic":"Implications - Economies of Scale","question":"Avoiding wasteful overlap of resources and personnel by consolidating data and applications across departments describes:","options":["Economies of scale","CPU thermal throttling","RAM memory fragmentation","Display resolution scaling"],"correct":0,"explanation":"التفسير بالعامية: دمج البيانات والتطبيقات وتجنب الهدر والتكرار في الموارد والموظفين عبر الأقسام هو تعريف الـ Economies of scale في السلايد 29.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=2"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:1","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is the primary definition of 'Data Abstraction' in database systems?","options":["Encrypting all database data files using symmetric keys","Suppression of details of data organization and storage, while highlighting essential features","Duplicating tables across multiple servers for load balancing","Converting relational tables into unstructured text files"],"correct":1,"explanation":"تجريد البيانات (Data Abstraction) هو إخفاء تفاصيل التخزين والتنظيم الفيزيائي وإبراز الخصائص الجوهرية الأساسية فقط.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:2","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"Which of the following describes a 'Data Model' according to the course slides?","options":["A collection of concepts that describe the structure of a database and provide means to achieve data abstraction","A physical silicon chip inside the hard disk drive controller","A network communication cable protocol","A graphics design tool used for creating user avatars"],"correct":0,"explanation":"نموذج البيانات هو مجموعة من المفاهيم الهيكلية التي تصف بنية قاعدة البيانات وتوفر الوسيلة لتحقيق تجريد البيانات.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:3","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"In a data model, what is the 'dynamic aspect or behavior' of a database application represented by?","options":["Disk motor RPM speed","Basic operations (retrievals and updates) and valid user-defined operations","Network cable bandwidth latency","Server room air conditioning temperature"],"correct":1,"explanation":"السلوك الديناميكي لقاعدة البيانات يتمثل في العمليات الأساسية (الاسترجاع والتحديث) والعمليات المعرفة من المستخدم مثل COMPUTE_GPA.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:4","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"Which category of data models is 'close to the way many users perceive data'?","options":["Low-level / Physical data models","High-level or Conceptual data models","Storage definition language models","Operating system kernel models"],"correct":1,"explanation":"النماذج المفاهيمية عالية المستوى (Conceptual models) هي الأقرب لطريقة إدراك وفهم المستخدمين للبيانات في العالم الواقعي.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:5","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"Which category of data models describes details of record formats, orderings, and access paths on storage media?","options":["Conceptual data models","Physical / Low-level data models","View definition models","Entity-Relationship models"],"correct":1,"explanation":"النماذج الفيزيائية منخفضة المستوى (Physical data models) هي التي تصف تفاصيل أشكال السجلات وترتيبها ومسارات التخزين على الوسائط.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:6","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"Why are Relational data models also called 'record-based' data models?","options":["Because they represent data by using record structures (tables of rows)","Because they can only record audio and speech data","Because they prevent records from ever being modified","Because they do not require any memory"],"correct":0,"explanation":"تسمى Record-based لأنها تمثل البيانات باستخدام هياكل السجلات (جداول مكونة من صفوف وسجلات).","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:7","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is an 'Access Path' in physical database modeling?","options":["The physical hallway path taken by database administrators to enter the server room","A structure that makes the search for particular database records efficient","An encrypted SSL connection between client and router","A backup copy of database transaction logs"],"correct":1,"explanation":"مسار الوصول (Access Path) هو هيكل منظم (زي الفهرس) يجعل البحث عن السجلات داخل قاعدة البيانات سريعاً وفعالاً.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:8","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"An 'Index' in a database is an example of what concept?","options":["A high-level conceptual entity","An access path that allows direct access to data using an index term or keyword","An external user interface dialog box","A hardware graphics pipeline processor"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الفهرس (Index) هو أبرز مثال على مسارات الوصول (Access path) ويتيح الوصول المباشر للسجلات باستخدام قيمة مفتاحية.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:9","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is a 'Database Schema'?","options":["The dynamic content of the database at 5:00 PM today","The description of a database specified during design, which is not expected to change frequently","The compiled binary file of the operating system","A query used to delete all rows from a table"],"correct":1,"explanation":"سكيما قاعدة البيانات هي الوصف والتصميم المحدد أثناء مرحلة البناء، ومن المتوقع ألا تتغير إلا نادراً جداً.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:10","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What does a 'Schema Diagram' display?","options":["The actual populated rows and individual student names","The structure of each record type but not the actual instances of records","The physical disk tracks and sectors allocated to files","The real-time CPU utilization graph"],"correct":1,"explanation":"مخطط السكيما يعرض هيكل كل نوع سجل فقط (أسماء الجداول والأعمدة) ولا يعرض السجلات الحقيقية أو البيانات الفعلية.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:11","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is a 'Schema Construct'?","options":["A brick used in the data center building","Each object in the schema, such as STUDENT or COURSE","A SQL syntax error during execution","A hardware hard drive failure"],"correct":1,"explanation":"كل كائن أو عنصر مفرد داخل السكيما (مثل جدول STUDENT أو جدول COURSE) يسمى Schema Construct.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:12","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is the 'Database State' (also called database instance or snapshot)?","options":["The state of the power supply voltage","The actual data stored in the database at a particular moment in time","The original design document approved by management","The programming language compiler version"],"correct":1,"explanation":"حالة قاعدة البيانات (Database State) هي البيانات الفعلية المخزنة في النظام في لحظة زمنية معينة.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:13","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is an 'Initial Database State'?","options":["The database state when it is initially loaded into the system","A database that has crashed and lost all its data","The state where no schema has been created yet","A backup archive stored on tape"],"correct":0,"explanation":"الحالة الابتدائية هي حالة قاعدة البيانات عند تحميل البيانات إليها لأول مرة بعد مرحلة الإنشاء.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:14","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is a 'Valid State' in database management?","options":["A state that has been encrypted with SHA-256","A state that satisfies the structure and constraints of the database","A state where all tables have zero rows","A state that is only accessible to system root administrators"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الحالة الصالحة (Valid State) هي الحالة التي تحقق وتلبي كافة القيود الهيكلية وقواعد النزاهة المحددة لقاعدة البيانات.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:15","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"In database terminology, the Schema is called ______ and the State is called ______:","options":["Extension, Intension","Intension, Extension","Hardware, Software","Internal, External"],"correct":1,"explanation":"السكيما تسمى رسمياً Intension (الهيكل والقصد)، بينما الحالة تسمى Extension (البيانات والامتداد الفعلي).","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:16","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is 'Schema Evolution'?","options":["The automatic deletion of old database tables every month","Changes applied to the schema as application requirements change over time","Upgrading the server power supply unit","The transformation of SQL into machine bytecode"],"correct":1,"explanation":"تطور السكيما (Schema Evolution) هو التعديلات التي يتم إدخالها على هيكل السكيما نتيجة لتغير متطلبات التطبيق مع مرور الوقت.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:17","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is the primary goal of the Three-Schema Architecture?","options":["To merge all application programs into a single executable file","To separate user applications from the physical database","To replace relational databases with flat text files","To eliminate the need for schema mappings"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الهدف الأسمى لمعمارية المستويات الثلاثة هو فصل تطبيقات المستخدمين عن قاعدة البيانات الفيزيائية وطرق تخزينها.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:18","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"Which level of the three-schema architecture describes the physical storage structure and access paths?","options":["External Level","Conceptual Level","Internal Level","Application Level"],"correct":2,"explanation":"المستوى الداخلي (Internal Level) هو الذي يصف الهيكل الفيزيائي للتخزين ومسارات الوصول على وسائط التخزين.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:19","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"Which level of the three-schema architecture describes the whole database structure for a community of users while hiding physical details?","options":["Internal Level","Conceptual Level","External Level","Physical Level"],"correct":1,"explanation":"المستوى المفاهيمي (Conceptual Level) يصف هيكل قاعدة البيانات بالكامل لجميع المستخدمين ويخفي التفاصيل الفيزيائية.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:20","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"Which level of the three-schema architecture describes the part of the database a particular user group is interested in while hiding the rest?","options":["Internal Level","Conceptual Level","External or View Level","Storage Level"],"correct":2,"explanation":"المستوى الخارجي (External/View Level) يصف فقط الجزء الذي يهم فئة معينة من المستخدمين ويحجب باقي البيانات.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:21","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is 'Logical Data Independence'?","options":["The capacity to change the internal storage media without modifying the conceptual schema","The capacity to change the conceptual schema without having to change external schemas or application programs","The ability to run database queries without a CPU","The process of converting binary data into ASCII text"],"correct":1,"explanation":"استقلالية البيانات المنطقية هي القدرة على تعديل المخطط المفاهيمي (إضافة جداول أو حقول) دون الحاجة لتعديل الواجهات الخارجية أو البرامج.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:22","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"What is 'Physical Data Independence'?","options":["The capacity to change the internal schema without having to change the conceptual schema","The capacity to change external views without changing user passwords","The requirement to rewrite SQL queries whenever hard disk sectors change","The ability of users to physically unplug servers during queries"],"correct":0,"explanation":"استقلالية البيانات الفيزيائية هي القدرة على تعديل المخطط الداخلي (تغيير أقراص التخزين أو إضافة فهارس) دون المساس بالسكيما المفاهيمية.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:23","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"Which DBMS language is used to specify the internal schema (storage structure)?","options":["VDL (View Definition Language)","SDL (Storage Definition Language)","DML (Data Manipulation Language)","HTML (HyperText Markup Language)"],"correct":1,"explanation":"لغة تعريف التخزين SDL (Storage Definition Language) هي المخصصة لتحديد وضبط المخطط الداخلي (Internal schema).","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:24","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"Which DBMS language specifies user views and their mappings to the conceptual schema?","options":["VDL (View Definition Language)","SDL (Storage Definition Language)","DML (Data Manipulation Language)","BIOS (Basic Input Output System)"],"correct":0,"explanation":"لغة تعريف واجهات العرض VDL (View Definition Language) هي المسؤولة عن تحديد رؤى المستخدمين وربطها بالمخطط المفاهيمي.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:25","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"In a Centralized DBMS Architecture, where are the DBMS functionality, application programs, and UI processing executed?","options":["Distributed across edge client devices","Carried out entirely on one single machine (Mainframe)","Split equally across three separate database clouds","On printer spooler controllers"],"correct":1,"explanation":"في المعمارية المركزية، يتم تنفيذ كافة وظائف الـ DBMS والتطبيقات ومعالجة الواجهات بالكامل على جهاز مركزي واحد.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:26","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"In a basic client/server architecture, which server maintains the files of the client machines?","options":["Print Server","File Server","Web Cache Proxy","Audio Streamer"],"correct":1,"explanation":"خادم الملفات (File Server) هو المسؤول عن حفظ وإدارة وتأمين ملفات أجهزة العملاء.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:27","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"In a Two-Tier Client/Server Architecture for DBMSs, what does the Client machine handle?","options":["SQL query compilation and disk storage sector caching","User interface programs and application programs","High-voltage power distribution to disk arrays","Operating system kernel thread dispatching on the server"],"correct":1,"explanation":"في معمارية الطبقتين، يتولى جهاز العميل تشغيل برامج واجهات المستخدم وبرامج التطبيق (UI and Application programs).","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:28","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"In a Three-Tier Web Architecture, what is the role of the intermediate layer (Application Server or Web Server)?","options":["It only provides electrical power to the database server","It runs application programs and stores/enforces business rules between client and database","It acts as a physical replacement for RAM memory","It prevents all clients from accessing web pages"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الطبقة الوسيطة (Application/Web server) تشغل البرامج التطبيقية وتخزن وتطبق قواعد العمل (Business rules) وتفصل العميل عن الداتابيز.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:29","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"In Figure 2.7 (b), what are the three architectural tiers called from top to bottom?","options":["Client Layer -> File Layer -> Network Layer","Presentation Layer -> Business Logic Layer -> Database Services Layer","Hardware Layer -> Kernel Layer -> Compiler Layer","Input Layer -> Hidden Layer -> Output Layer"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الطبقات الثلاث في الشكل 2.7 (b) هي من الأعلى للأسفل: طبقة العرض (Presentation Layer)، طبقة منطق العمل (Business Logic Layer)، وطبقة خدمات الداتابيز (Database Services Layer).","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"},{"id":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3:30","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3","topic":"المحاضرة 3","question":"In the COMPANY ER diagram (Slide 7), how is a Weak Entity such as DEPENDENT represented?","options":["With a single oval","With a double rectangle","With a dashed diamond","With a thick single circle"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الكيان الضعيف (Weak Entity) مثل DEPENDENT يُمثل دائماً في مخطط الـ ER بمستطيل مزدوج (Double Rectangle).","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=database-systems&lecture=3"}],"operating-system":[{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01:roles-report","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Identify the application role in a concrete task.","question":"In the report example, which component provides the text-formatting functions?","options":["Hardware","Operating system","Application program","User"],"correct":2,"explanation":"بالضبط؛ Word هو الـApplication program اللي فيه أدوات الكتابة والتنسيق. الـCPU بينفّذ تعليماته.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01:users-machines","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Recognize non-human users in the source model.","question":"In this computer-system model, another computer can be a user.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ Users ممكن يبقوا أشخاص أو آلات أو أجهزة كمبيوتر تانية، زي ما سلايد 5 بيقول.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01:allocation-conflict","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Apply resource-allocation responsibility.","question":"A browser and a word processor request limited hardware resources. Who coordinates their use across the system?","options":["The browser","The operating system","The word processor","The user for every request"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ ده دور الـResource allocator: الـOS بيدير الطلبات على الموارد بكفاءة وعدل.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01:control-guarantee","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Distinguish control goals from an absolute guarantee.","question":"Being a control program guarantees that the OS prevents every program error.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ التحكم في تشغيل البرامج بيساعد يمنع الأخطاء وسوء الاستخدام. مش معناه إن الأخطاء مستحيلة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01:view-response","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Distinguish user and system viewpoints in a new observation.","question":"A student says, “I want the program to respond quickly and be easy to use.” Which view does this best express?","options":["User view: convenience and performance","System view: resolving resource conflicts","System view: controlling program execution","OS definition: what a vendor includes"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ الطالب عايز سهولة استخدام واستجابة سريعة. دي User view.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01:historical-kernel","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Identify the broad purpose of the kernel, not a single service.","question":"In the context of operating systems, what is the main purpose of a kernel?","options":["To provide a user interface for interacting with the system","To manage the system’s CPU, memory, and other hardware resources","To compile and execute user programs","To create and manage network connections"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ الدور الأساسي هنا إدارة CPU وmemory وباقي موارد الجهاز. ده حل مستقل، مش مفتاح إجابة رسمي.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01:bundle-kernel","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Diagnose the inference that shipped software must be kernel code.","question":"A student says, “This file utility came with the OS, so it must be part of the kernel.” Which reply best evaluates that reasoning?","options":["The vendor bundle alone determines whether a program is kernel code.","Every system program shipped with an OS belongs to its kernel.","Only application programs can exist outside the kernel.","System programs can ship with an OS while remaining outside its kernel."],"correct":3,"explanation":"صح؛ ممكن System program ييجي مع الـOS وهو برّه Kernel. وجوده مع النظام مش دليل إنه جزء من النواة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01:four-components-adapted","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Recall the four roles without replacing one by the kernel.","question":"Which list gives the four computer-system components in slides 4–5?","options":["CPU, RAM, storage, I/O devices","Hardware, kernel, system programs, applications","Hardware, OS, application programs, users","Users, user interface, applications, system programs"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ دي المكونات الأربعة في سلايد 5. الـKernel جزء من الـOS، مش مكوّن خامس.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-01"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-02:os-02-startup-order","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Order the source startup responsibilities.","question":"Which sequence matches the startup overview?","options":["Word runs → loads kernel → initializes hardware","Bootstrap runs → initializes system → loads and starts kernel","Kernel runs → creates firmware → power-up begins"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ ده ترتيب الأدوار في السلايد، حتى لو الجهاز الحقيقي فيه مراحل أكتر.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-02"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-02:os-02-kernel-first","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Distinguish early startup code from the kernel.","question":"The kernel must already be executing for the bootstrap program to begin.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"بالضبط؛ تعليمات البداية هي اللي تجهّز الطريق لتحميل Kernel وتشغيله.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-02"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-02:os-02-firmware-role","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Recognize firmware as persistent startup software.","question":"Why is firmware relevant before normal applications can run?","options":["It is the document currently open in Word","It means all programs are currently running in RAM","It supplies stored early startup instructions"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ تعليمات البداية لازم تكون متاحة قبل تشغيل Kernel والبرامج العادية.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-02"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-03:os-03-completion-vs-data","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Separate completion notification from data transfer.","question":"A controller has completed an I/O operation. What informs the CPU?","options":["An interrupt","The interrupt vector physically moves the data","The local buffer becomes main memory"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ ده إشعار الانتهاء. البيانات ليها مسار نقل منفصل في الرسم.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-03"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-03:os-03-concurrent","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Recognize concurrent CPU and device operation.","question":"In the source model, CPU execution and I/O device operation can overlap.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ CPU والجهاز يقدروا يتقدّموا في نفس الفترة، مع احتمال التنافس على الذاكرة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-03"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-03:os-03-vector","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Identify the function of an interrupt vector.","question":"What information does the interrupt vector provide in this overview?","options":["A list proving that another user process must run","Addresses of service routines","All bytes of the file being read"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ علشان التحكم يوصل لروتين الخدمة المناسب.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-03"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-03:os-03-trap-source","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Differentiate software-generated events from device completion.","question":"A trap or exception, as introduced in the slide, can result from a software error or a user request.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ ده وصف السلايد للأحداث الناتجة عن Software، مقابل إشعار من جهاز مثلاً.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-03"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-04:os-04-cache-miss","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Apply the cache miss path.","question":"Item A is absent from the cache. What follows in the source’s caching overview?","options":["Use A from cache without fetching it","Delete the slower storage because the cache replaces it","Fetch A from slower storage, copy it into cache, then use it"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ ده مسار Cache miss، مش فشل دائم في القراءة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-04"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-04:os-04-volatile","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Separate volatile and nonvolatile storage.","question":"Typical volatile main memory retains its contents after power is removed.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح اختيارك؛ الجملة غلط. RAM المعتادة مش حفظ دائم بعد فصل الكهرباء.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-04"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-04:os-04-driver-controller","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Distinguish driver software from controller hardware.","question":"Which component provides a uniform interface between a controller and the kernel?","options":["Device driver","Magnetic platter","A cache replacement decision"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ Driver برنامج بيدير I/O وبيخفي تفاصيل Controller عن الواجهة اللي Kernel بيتعامل معاها.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-04"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-04:os-04-hierarchy-tradeoff","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Recognize hierarchy tradeoffs without invented benchmarks.","question":"Why keep both a small fast cache and a larger slower store?","options":["A cache must be larger than everything it caches","All storage levels have identical speed and volatility","Use fast access for useful copies while retaining larger capacity elsewhere"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ بنوازن السرعة والتكلفة والمساحة، ومش بنفترض إن Cache يشيل كل البيانات.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-04"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-05:os-05-smp-work","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Interpret symmetric multiprocessing without lockstep confusion.","question":"In SMP, what does “each processor performs all tasks” mean in this introductory comparison?","options":["Each processor is necessarily a separate networked computer","Processors can perform the same types of work","Every processor must execute the identical instruction at the same instant"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ ده مقابل إسناد دور خاص لكل Processor في Asymmetric multiprocessing.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-05"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-05:os-05-core-is-node","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Distinguish dual-core chips from clusters.","question":"The two cores in the slide’s dual-core chip are two complete independent cluster computers.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح اختيارك؛ حدود Chip في سلايد 19 مختلفة عن حدود Computer nodes في سلايد 21.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-05"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-05:os-05-cluster-standby","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Recognize asymmetric clustering.","question":"A service runs on one computer while another waits in hot-standby mode. Which source description fits?","options":["Symmetric clustering with every node running applications","Two cores inside one chip","Asymmetric clustering"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ Node مستنية تتولى الدور لو احتجناها.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-05"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-05:os-05-hpc-requirement","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Recognize the application requirement for parallel HPC.","question":"What is needed for an application to exploit an HPC cluster’s parallel computation?","options":["All nodes must be cores on the same chip","The application must be designed to use parallelization","No software change is ever needed because a network divides all code"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ وجود Nodes أكتر لوحده مش بيقسّم أي برنامج تلقائيًا.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-05"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-05:os-05-throughput","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Distinguish system throughput from single-job speed.","question":"A potential increase in throughput guarantees that every individual program finishes twice as fast.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"بالضبط؛ Throughput الأعلى لا يثبت تسريع كل برنامج مرتين.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-05"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-06:os-06-waiting-job","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Apply multiprogramming to an I/O wait.","question":"On one CPU, A waits for I/O and B is ready in memory. Which action supports multiprogramming’s efficiency goal?","options":["Run B while A waits","Require the CPU to remain idle until A finishes I/O","Execute A’s and B’s instructions simultaneously on that one CPU"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ نستغل CPU في Job جاهزة بدل ما يفضل مستني I/O الخاص بـA.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-06"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-06:os-06-all-memory-running","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Distinguish residency from simultaneous execution.","question":"Every job shown in the source’s memory-layout diagram must be executing on the CPU at the same instant.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"بالضبط؛ موجودة في Memory مش معناها Running كلها في نفس اللحظة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-06"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-06:os-06-interactive","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Recognize time sharing’s purpose.","question":"Which description best captures time sharing?","options":["Keep the whole system permanently below one second for every task","Switch CPU work frequently enough to support interactive use","Finish every job before accepting any interaction from another"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ بنقسّم فرص التشغيل علشان المستخدمين يقدروا يتفاعلوا.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-06"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-06:os-06-virtual-memory","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Interpret the introductory virtual-memory claim.","question":"Virtual memory allows a process to execute without its entire program being resident in main memory at once.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ ده وصف السلايد. الأجزاء المطلوبة للتنفيذ لسه لازم تبقى متاحة وقت استخدامها.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-06"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-07:os-07-same-process","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Separate mode transition from process switching.","question":"A makes a system call, the kernel serves it, and A resumes. Which change is demonstrated?","options":["A guaranteed switch from A to B","No mode transition because the process name stayed A","A mode transition, with no required switch to another process"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ دخلنا Kernel ورجعنا لـA نفسها. Process switch يحتاج إننا نكمل Process مختلفة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-07"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-07:os-07-privileged-user","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Identify enforcement of privileged operations.","question":"A normal user-mode program may directly execute every privileged instruction.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح اختيارك؛ Hardware بيفرض الفرق، والبرنامج يطلب الخدمات المناسبة بدل تنفيذ التعليمات الحساسة بحرّيته.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-07"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-07:os-07-timer-expiry","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Identify the consequence of timer expiry.","question":"In the slide’s timer model, what happens when the counter reaches zero?","options":["An interrupt lets the OS regain control","The application automatically receives kernel privileges forever","The computer must terminate every running program"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ OS بعد كده يقرّر التصرف المناسب.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-07"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-07:os-07-timer-user-reset","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Explain why timer setup is privileged.","question":"Allowing any user-mode process to freely reset the timer could undermine the OS’s ability to regain control.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ برنامج ممكن يؤجّل Interrupt باستمرار. علشان كده ضبط Timer عملية Privileged في السلايد.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-07"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08:os-08-management-map","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Match memory allocation to the correct responsibility.","question":"The OS records which process owns a used memory region and frees it when no longer needed. Which responsibility is this?","options":["Formatting text inside Word","Memory management","File-name creation only"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ تتبّع الاستخدام وAllocation وDeallocation من مسؤوليات Memory management.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08:os-08-suspend-delete","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Distinguish suspending from deleting a process.","question":"Suspending a process necessarily deletes it, so it cannot later resume.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"بالضبط؛ الإيقاف المؤقت غير الحذف، وإلا Resume ما كانش هيبقى له معنى هنا.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08:os-08-file-abstraction","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Identify the logical file abstraction.","question":"Why can a user open notes.txt without specifying physical disk tracks?","options":["Every file is permanently stored only in a CPU register","A directory removes the need for any storage device","The file system maps logical files onto secondary storage"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ واجهة File بتخفي تفاصيل الوسيط، والـOS يدير الربط بالتخزين.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08:os-08-bandwidth-vs-latency","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Distinguish access time from data-transfer rate.","question":"Which property describes how much data can be transferred per unit of time?","options":["Access time alone","Bandwidth","Capacity alone"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ كمية بيانات لكل فترة. Access time عن زمن الوصول، وCapacity عن المساحة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08:os-08-stale-copy","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Recognize the cache-coherency problem.","question":"CPU 0 updates A, while CPU 1 holds an older cached copy. What must the system avoid?","options":["Using the stale copy as though it were the valid current value","Ever letting any CPU cache contain different addresses","Using cache at all because all cached data is permanently invalid"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ وجود نسخة سريعة مش كفاية. Coherency تنسّق الصلاحية أو التحديث.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08:os-08-dated-table","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"الفصل 1","topic":"Read dated numerical examples with appropriate limits.","question":"The 2013 slide’s example storage capacities establish permanent maximum capacities for all computers.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح اختيارك؛ نتعلم معنى المقارنة من غير تحويل أمثلة 2013 لحدود Hardware ثابتة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-08"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09:os-09-save","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Identify file-system manipulation in a familiar scenario.","question":"A student creates report.txt, then searches for it. Which service best matches these file operations?","options":["Accounting","File-system manipulation","Authentication","Resource allocation"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ إنشاء ملف والبحث عنه من خدمات File system.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09:os-09-usage","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Separate accounting from allocation.","question":"The lab records how much CPU time each account used. Which service is this?","options":["Communications","Program execution","Accounting","Error detection"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ Accounting بتتابع نوع وكمية الموارد اللي كل مستخدم استخدمها.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09:os-09-network","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Recognize network communication between processes.","question":"Two programs exchange information between computers over a network. Which service is most directly involved?","options":["Communications","Authentication only","File deletion only","Accounting only"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ تبادل البيانات بين العمليات عبر الشبكة مثال Communications في السلايد.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09:os-09-permission","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Distinguish identity checks from resource permissions.","question":"The OS verifies a login identity. Which term directly names this check?","options":["Resource allocation","Authentication","I/O completion","File search"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ Authentication بتتحقق إنك الشخص أو الحساب اللي بتقول عليه.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09:os-09-gui","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Interpret interfaces in the source service map.","question":"A GUI is a way for a user to interact with the system.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ GUI واجهة بأزرار ونوافذ، ومن طرق التعامل في سلايد 4.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09:os-09-guarantee","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Separate error-handling responsibility from perfect repair.","question":"Error detection guarantees that every detected error will be repaired.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ ممكن التعامل يكون بإبلاغ البرنامج بالفشل. Error detection مش ضمان إصلاح كل خطأ.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09:os-09-one-service","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Recognize that services may participate in the same operation.","question":"Reading a file can involve both file-system services and I/O operations.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ تنظيم الملف ونقل البيانات من الجهاز ممكن يشتركوا في نفس القراءة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-09"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10:os-10-api-contract","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Identify what an API specifies.","question":"What does an API tell a programmer?","options":["Every internal kernel algorithm","Available functions, parameters, and expected return values","The physical address of every device","Only the graphical appearance of a window"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ الدوال والمدخلات والنتائج المتوقعة هي عقد استخدام API.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10:os-10-every-api","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Reject a one-to-one API/system-call assumption.","question":"Every API function directly invokes exactly one system call.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ API بتحدد واجهة استخدام، مش ضمان إن كل دالة تعمل System call واحدة مباشرة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10:os-10-short-read","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Interpret a successful read result without confusing data and count.","question":"In the regular-file example, read(fd, buf, 100) returns 40. What does 40 mean?","options":["The file descriptor is 40","40 bytes were read into buf","40 bytes remain to be read","The buffer address is 40"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ count حد أقصى، والنتيجة بتقول كام byte اتقرا فعلًا.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10:os-10-read-error","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Recognize the read error indicator.","question":"In this read() example, which return value indicates an error?","options":["0","A positive byte count","-1","The address of buf"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ -1 مؤشر خطأ في الواجهة المعروضة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10:os-10-call-number","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Explain indexed system-call dispatch.","question":"In the source implementation model, what is the system-call number used for?","options":["Selecting a table entry for the requested service","Providing the address of the parameter table","Replacing the caller with another process every time","Counting the bytes already read"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ الواجهة تستخدم الرقم كـIndex للمدخل المناسب في جدول النداءات.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10:os-10-same-process","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Separate mode transition from switching processes.","question":"Entering kernel mode for a system call can return to the same process.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ الرسم بيفترض الرجوع لنفس المستدعي. تغيير الصلاحية مش بالضرورة تبديل Process.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10:os-10-table","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Interpret the table address passed in a register.","question":"In slide 11, a register contains X. What is X?","options":["All parameter values compressed into one number","The address of the parameter table","The number of all running programs","The result of every system call"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ النظام يستخدم X علشان يوصل للـParameters في الذاكرة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10:os-10-unlimited","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Understand the bounded advantage of memory-based argument passing.","question":"Block and stack methods remove every possible memory limit on parameters.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ عبارة السلايد عن عدم التقييد مقصود بيها حد Registers، مش ذاكرة غير محدودة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10:os-10-library-boundary","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Locate the privilege transition in the library example.","question":"In the illustrated printf-to-write path, which event requires entry into the kernel?","options":["Calling an ordinary formatting function in user space","The system-call entry for the OS write service","Including stdio.h","Declaring main()"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ طلب خدمة write عن طريق System call هو عبور الحد في الرسم.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10:os-10-printf-once","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Avoid a false immediate one-to-one printf/write rule.","question":"One printf() call must always cause one immediate write() system call.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ printf دالة Library، ومش لازم يبقى فيه write واحدة فورية لكل نداء.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-10"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-11:os-11-which-snapshot","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Read the FreeBSD snapshot without inferring timing.","question":"What does the FreeBSD snapshot directly show?","options":["Several processes present with the kernel and interpreter","A measured CPU schedule for three cores","Only one user program can be resident","Exact memory addresses for each process"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ ده اللي مربعات Process B وC وD بتوضحه. توقيت التنفيذ مش مرسوم.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-11"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-11:os-11-msdos-start","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Compare startup and running-program snapshots.","question":"In the source MS-DOS example, what changes when a program runs?","options":["The kernel is replaced by the user process","A process occupies part of the formerly free memory","The interpreter is replaced completely by the user process","The program is loaded without reducing the formerly free region"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ لقطة (b) فيها Process ومساحة حرة أقل، مع Kernel وInterpreter.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-11"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-11:os-11-parallel","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Separate a memory map from evidence of parallel execution.","question":"Three process boxes in memory prove that three processes execute CPU instructions at the same instant.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ ممكن العمليات تتشارك Core واحد على أدوار. خريطة الذاكرة مش جدول تنفيذ.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-11"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-11:os-11-historical","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Keep the platform example bounded.","question":"Slide 13 is a simplified historical platform comparison, not a specification for every current operating system.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ المصدر من 2013 وبيستخدم MS-DOS وFreeBSD كأمثلة محددة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-11"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12:os-12-organization","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Recognize what an OS organization model describes.","question":"Two systems offer similar services but arrange their responsibilities differently. What does an OS-structure comparison focus on?","options":["How responsibilities and interfaces are arranged","How resource consumption is recorded for each user","The execution order of processes on a CPU timeline","The occupied regions in one system-memory snapshot"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ بنقارن مكان الخدمات وحدودها وطريقة تواصلها.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12:os-12-simple-path","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Explain a consequence of weak separation.","question":"In the classic MS-DOS model, why is direct hardware access a protection concern?","options":["It guarantees every program is safe","It weakens centralized control of access","It turns every program into a microkernel","It requires every service to run in a user-space server"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ تجاوز حدود منظمة يقلّل قدرة النظام على التحكم في الوصول.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12:os-12-mono-services","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Locate services in the traditional UNIX model.","question":"Where are file-system, scheduling, and memory-management functions in the traditional UNIX model shown?","options":["In user-side system programs above the system-call interface","Inside the kernel below the system-call interface","In a standard library above the system-call interface","In separate user-space service servers"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ ده تجمع وظائف كتير داخل Kernel الكبير في Monolithic.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12:os-12-rows-layers","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Avoid interpreting every stacked drawing as strict layering.","question":"The rows in the traditional UNIX picture prove that it is fully layered.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ مظهر الرسم مش كفاية؛ المهم قواعد اعتماد الخدمات على بعض.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12:os-12-layer-rule","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Apply the lower-layer dependency rule.","question":"Which dependency follows the source layered model?","options":["A layer uses a service from a lower layer","Every layer bypasses lower layers and directly uses hardware","A lower layer always requires the top UI to operate","All layers must run as separate user processes"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ كل Layer تستخدم خدمات مستويات أقل حسب التنظيم المحدد.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12:os-12-layer-debug","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Qualify the layer-local debugging statement.","question":"An error observed in a layer proves that all lower layers are correct, even when they were never tested.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ مكان ظهور المشكلة وحده مش دليل صحة الطبقات اللي تحتها.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12:os-12-micro-overhead","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Identify the source microkernel communication tradeoff.","question":"Which cost is emphasized for the microkernel model?","options":["Communication overhead across user/kernel boundaries","No way to add new services","All file services must be inside the kernel","No communication between components"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ الرسائل والعبور بين User وKernel ممكن يضيفوا تكلفة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12:os-12-module-place","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Distinguish kernel modules from microkernel user-space services.","question":"Where does a loadable kernel module run in this model?","options":["As an ordinary user-space server by definition","Inside the kernel when loaded","In a user-side library linked to an application","In firmware that runs before the kernel starts"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ Module تنظم الكود وتتحمل حسب الحاجة، لكنها لسه كود Kernel.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12:os-12-module-isolation","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Avoid equating modularity with user-space fault isolation.","question":"A loadable kernel module has the same user-space isolation as the file server in the microkernel diagram.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ فصل الكود لModules مش هو نفسه فصل الصلاحيات والمساحات في مثال Microkernel.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12:os-12-hybrid-label","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"الفصل 2","topic":"Interpret a mixed-design classification carefully.","question":"A system includes ideas from Mach and other approaches. What is the best conclusion from this information alone?","options":["It must be a pure microkernel","It cannot contain kernel modules","Its components must be inspected before claiming a pure organization","All its services must run outside the kernel"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ Hybrid يجمع اتجاهات، ومكان كل خدمة محتاج تفاصيل النظام.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-12"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-13:os-13-instances","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Two users start the same executable. Which statement can be true?","question":"Two users start the same executable. Which statement can be true?","options":["There can be two processes for one program.","The program can have only one process.","Both processes must have the same current execution state."],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ نفس الـProgram ممكن يبقى ليه أكتر من Process، وكل واحدة لها حالة تنفيذ.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-13"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-13:os-13-call-data","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"In this introductory model, where do function return addresses belong?","question":"In this introductory model, where do function return addresses belong?","options":["Text section","Stack","Heap"],"correct":1,"explanation":"بالضبط؛ Stack بتحتفظ ببيانات الدوال المؤقتة ومنها عنوان الرجوع.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-13"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-13:os-13-next-instruction","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Which records the location of the next instruction to execute?","question":"Which records the location of the next instruction to execute?","options":["Program counter","Executable filename","Global variable section"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ Program counter بيحدد مكان التعليمة الجاية، وهو جزء من حالة التنفيذ.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-13"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-13:os-13-passive","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"An executable stored on disk is already an active process.","question":"An executable stored on disk is already an active process.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ ده Program محفوظ. Process هي حالة البرنامج وقت التشغيل.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-13"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-14:os-14-io-complete","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"A waiting process finishes its I/O. In the five-state graph, what is its next state?","question":"A waiting process finishes its I/O. In the five-state graph, what is its next state?","options":["Running immediately","Ready","New"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ الحدث خلص فترجع Ready، وبعد Dispatch ممكن تبقى Running.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-14"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-14:os-14-resume-record","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Which PCB information helps resume at the correct instruction?","question":"Which PCB information helps resume at the correct instruction?","options":["Program counter and CPU registers","Only the executable filename","Only the number of open files"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ مكان التعليمة والقيم المحفوظة يساعدوا في استكمال التنفيذ.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-14"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-14:os-14-mode-is-switch","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Every return from kernel mode must resume a different process.","question":"Every return from kernel mode must resume a different process.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ ممكن نفس A تدخل Kernel وتكمل. Context switch بين Processes يحتاج تبديل من A إلى B.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-14"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-14:os-14-overhead","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"During save/restore for a process switch, what is the CPU doing?","question":"During save/restore for a process switch, what is the CPU doing?","options":["Application work for both processes at once","Necessary OS work rather than the processes’ application work","Nothing at all"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ ده شغل OS لازم، لكن محسوب Overhead بالنسبة لتقدم شغل التطبيقات.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-14"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-15:os-15-thread-pc","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"A process gains a second thread. What must the model now track?","question":"A process gains a second thread. What must the model now track?","options":["Only one execution location for both threads","Execution details, including a program counter, for each thread","A second copy of the whole operating system"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ تعدد Threads محتاج تفاصيل تنفيذ لكل مسار، ومنها Program counter.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-15"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-15:os-15-threads-parallel","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Having two threads guarantees simultaneous execution on one CPU.","question":"Having two threads guarantees simultaneous execution on one CPU.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ على CPU واحدة المسارات ممكن تتبادل التنفيذ. العدد وحده مش دليل Parallel execution.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-15"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-15:os-15-record-parent","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"In the historical Linux illustration, which information describes the process family relationship?","question":"In the historical Linux illustration, which information describes the process family relationship?","options":["parent and children","files only","mm only"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ parent وchildren روابط علاقة الإنشاء بين العمليات في المثال.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-15"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-15:os-15-historical-fields","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"The task_struct field list on the 2013 slide is a guaranteed current Linux layout.","question":"The task_struct field list on the 2013 slide is a guaranteed current Linux layout.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ نستخدمها لتفسير أنواع المعلومات. تفاصيل Linux تتغير، والسلايد مش مواصفة إصدار حالي.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-15"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-16:os-16-which-queue","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"A process cannot proceed until its disk I/O completes. Which queue fits this reason for waiting?","question":"A process cannot proceed until its disk I/O completes. Which queue fits this reason for waiting?","options":["Ready queue","Device queue","The CPU itself"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ سبب الانتظار I/O device، فمكانها Device queue في النموذج.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-16"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-16:os-16-cpu-selection","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Which scheduler makes the frequent decision about the next ready process to execute?","question":"Which scheduler makes the frequent decision about the next ready process to execute?","options":["Long-term scheduler","Medium-term scheduler","Short-term scheduler"],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ Short-term أو CPU scheduler بيختار من الجاهزين، وقراره متكرر فلازم سريع.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-16"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-16:os-16-swap-exit","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Swapping a process out of memory means that the process has terminated.","question":"Swapping a process out of memory means that the process has terminated.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ Swapping إخراج مؤقت للديسك مع إمكانية الرجوع واستكمال التنفيذ.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-16"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-16:os-16-bound-pattern","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Which pattern best matches an I/O-bound process in this model?","question":"Which pattern best matches an I/O-bound process in this model?","options":["Many short CPU bursts separated by I/O","No CPU use at all","Few very long computation bursts"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ I/O بياخد وقت أكبر، وبتحتاج CPU لفترات قصيرة متكررة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-16"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-16:os-16-fork-always-waits","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Creating a child always forces the parent to wait for that child.","question":"Creating a child always forces the parent to wait for that child.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ مسار الانتظار في الرسم حالة ممكنة. Parent ممكن يكمل بالتزامن أو يختار الانتظار.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-16"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-17:os-17-historical-conclusion","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"What is a justified conclusion from this 2013 slide?","question":"What is a justified conclusion from this 2013 slide?","options":["All current mobile systems enforce exactly these limits.","Foreground visibility and background execution permission are different ideas.","Every hidden application is executing without limits."],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ الواجهة ممكن تختفي لكن التنفيذ يعتمد على نوع المهمة وسياسة النظام.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-17"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-17:os-17-hidden-suspended","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"In the historical example, every process not shown on the display must be suspended.","question":"In the historical example, every process not shown on the display must be suspended.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ السلايد بيدي أمثلة Background tasks مسموحة زي Audio playback.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-17"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-17:os-17-service-ui","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"In the slide’s Android example, what is the role of a service?","question":"In the slide’s Android example, what is the role of a service?","options":["A UI window for the foreground user","Background work without a user interface","Proof that a fully suspended process continues executing its own code"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ الفكرة شغل Background بلا UI. تفاصيل الحدود الحديثة مش موضوع السلايد.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-17"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-17:os-17-current-policy","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"The 2013 comparison establishes current Android background restrictions.","question":"The 2013 comparison establishes current Android background restrictions.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ ده مثال تاريخي. أي سؤال عن سياسة إصدار حالي يحتاج مصدر حديث لذلك الإصدار.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-17"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18:os-18-fork-results","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"After successful fork(), what does the parent receive as the return value?","question":"After successful fork(), what does the parent receive as the return value?","options":["0","The new child’s PID","The parent’s own PID"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ Parent بتاخد PID الخاص بالـChild الجديدة، وChild بتاخد 0.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18:os-18-exec-identity","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Child PID C successfully calls exec. What changes?","question":"Child PID C successfully calls exec. What changes?","options":["Its program image changes; PID C remains.","It creates another child PID automatically.","It becomes the parent process."],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ exec استبدال داخل نفس Caller. عملية الإنشاء كانت fork قبلها في المثال.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18:os-18-fork-failure","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"In the slide’s code, fork returns a negative value. Which branch applies?","question":"In the slide’s code, fork returns a negative value. Which branch applies?","options":["The child executes ls.","The parent waits for the newly created child.","The error branch reports failure; this call created no child."],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ القيمة السالبة تدخل فرع الخطأ، ومش بنفترض وجود Child من الطلب ده.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18:os-18-wait-always-blocks","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"A successful wait must always spend time blocked before returning.","question":"A successful wait must always spend time blocked before returning.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ لو Child انتهت وحالتها متاحة، wait ممكن ترجع فورًا بالمعلومات.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18:os-18-windows-creation","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Which call creates the process in the slide’s Windows example?","question":"Which call creates the process in the slide’s Windows example?","options":["CreateProcess","WaitForSingleObject","CloseHandle"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ CreateProcess طلب الإنشاء. الانتظار وإغلاق الـHandles وظائف منفصلة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18:os-18-live-zombie","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"A still-running child is a zombie simply because its parent has not called wait.","question":"A still-running child is a zombie simply because its parent has not called wait.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ Zombie في النموذج المعتاد Child انتهت ولسه حالتها مااتجمعتش.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18:os-18-orphan-case","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"A child remains alive after its original parent exits. What is the relevant introductory term?","question":"A child remains alive after its original parent exits. What is the relevant introductory term?","options":["Zombie solely because wait was not called","Orphan","A successful exec"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ Orphan فقدت Parent الأصلي. في Linux تتربط بـParent بديل حسب النظام.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18:os-18-cascading-universal","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Every operating system must terminate all children when a parent exits.","question":"Every operating system must terminate all children when a parent exits.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ Cascading termination سياسة لبعض الأنظمة، مش قانون عام لكل OS.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18:os-18-fork-order","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Assume fork and wait succeed, with one child. What ordering does the parent’s code establish?","question":"Assume fork and wait succeed, with one child. What ordering does the parent’s code establish?","options":["The parent must execute before the child.","The child must execute before the parent.","The parent prints Child Complete after wait has collected the child’s termination."],"correct":2,"explanation":"صح؛ في افتراض النجاح وChild واحدة، الطباعة بعد wait الناجحة مرتبطة بانتهاء Child.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-18"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19:os-19-cooperation-example","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Process A produces data used by process B. Which description fits?","question":"Process A produces data used by process B. Which description fits?","options":["Cooperating processes","Independent processes by definition","A guarantee of faster execution"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ فيه تأثير وتبادل بيانات، فده تعاون محتاج IPC.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19:os-19-shared-coordinate","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"A shared-memory consumer may read before the producer finishes writing. What is missing?","question":"A shared-memory consumer may read before the producer finishes writing. What is missing?","options":["A longer executable filename","Synchronization of their access","A guarantee of unbounded physical RAM"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ الوصول لنفس المساحة محتاج تنسيق عشان البيانات تكون جاهزة قبل قراءتها.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19:os-19-message-ops","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Which pair describes the IPC operations in the message-passing model?","question":"Which pair describes the IPC operations in the message-passing model?","options":["fork and exec","send and receive","open and rename"],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ لازم رابط اتصال وتبادل باستخدام send وreceive.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19:os-19-shared-no-os","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Shared-memory data exchange means the OS has no role in setting up or protecting the shared region.","question":"Shared-memory data exchange means the OS has no role in setting up or protecting the shared region.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ تحكم User processes في التبادل بعد التجهيز لا يلغي دور OS في إعداد وحماية الذاكرة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19:os-19-empty-receive","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"No message is available. What does a non-blocking receive do in the slide’s model?","question":"No message is available. What does a non-blocking receive do in the slide’s model?","options":["It waits until a message arrives.","It returns an indication that no message is available.","It terminates the sender."],"correct":1,"explanation":"صح؛ يرجع نتيجة زي Null message بدل الانتظار، حسب واجهة النموذج.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19:os-19-bounded-full","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"A bounded link has two slots, both full. In the slide’s capacity model, what must a third send wait for?","question":"A bounded link has two slots, both full. In the slide’s capacity model, what must a third send wait for?","options":["A free buffer slot","A new PID for the sender","The receiver to terminate"],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ المشكلة امتلاء الطابور. استقبال رسالة يقدر يفضّي مكان في المثال.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19:os-19-unbounded-all-waits","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"An unbounded buffer cancels the receive condition of a separately specified blocking send.","question":"An unbounded buffer cancels the receive condition of a separately specified blocking send.","options":["True · صح","False · غلط"],"correct":1,"explanation":"غلط؛ السعة تمنع انتظار الامتلاء، لكن Blocking send ممكن يفضل مرتبط باستقبال الرسالة حسب الواجهة.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19"},{"id":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19:os-19-rendezvous","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"الفصل 3","topic":"Which source-model combination is described as a rendezvous?","question":"Which source-model combination is described as a rendezvous?","options":["Both send and receive are blocking.","Every non-blocking receive, even with no sender.","Any buffer that has at least one free slot."],"correct":0,"explanation":"صح؛ الطرفان يتقابلوا للتبادل في تعريف السلايد. Zero capacity كمان يحتاج لقاء مباشر.","sourceUrl":"education-preview/os/index.html?unit=os-19"}],"computer-graphics":[{"id":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics:cg-q1","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Graphics Pipeline","topic":"Computer Graphics vs Image Processing","question":"What is the fundamental difference between Computer Graphics and Image Processing?","options":["Computer Graphics synthesizes images from geometric models, while Image Processing analyzes or transforms existing images","Computer Graphics only works in 2D, while Image Processing works in 3D","Image Processing creates 3D meshes from scratch","They are completely identical processes"],"correct":0,"explanation":"رسوميات الحاسوب (Computer Graphics) تبدأ من بيانات ونماذج هندسية لتوليد صورة، بينما معالجة الصور (Image Processing) تبدأ من صورة موجودة لتحسينها أو استخراج معلومات منها.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics"},{"id":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics:cg-q2","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Displays & Frame Buffer","topic":"Frame Buffer Calculation","question":"How many megabytes (MB) are required for a Frame Buffer of resolution 1024 × 768 with 24 bits per pixel (True Color)?","options":["1.5 MB","2.25 MB","3.0 MB","6.0 MB"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الحجم بالبايت = 1024 × 768 × (24 / 8) = 1024 × 768 × 3 بايت. بالقسمة على (1024 × 1024) = (768 × 3) / 1024 = 2.25 MB.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics"},{"id":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics:cg-q3","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: DDA & Bresenham Line","topic":"DDA Algorithm","question":"Using the DDA line algorithm to draw a line from (2, 3) to (12, 8), how many steps are required and what are (x_inc, y_inc)?","options":["steps = 5, x_inc = 2, y_inc = 1","steps = 10, x_inc = 1, y_inc = 0.5","steps = 10, x_inc = 0.5, y_inc = 1","steps = 12, x_inc = 1, y_inc = 1"],"correct":1,"explanation":"dx = 12 - 2 = 10، و dy = 8 - 3 = 5. عدد الخطوات steps = max(|10|, |5|) = 10. إذن x_inc = 10/10 = 1، و y_inc = 5/10 = 0.5.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics"},{"id":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics:cg-q4","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: DDA & Bresenham Line","topic":"Bresenham Initial Decision Parameter","question":"In Bresenham's Line Drawing Algorithm for a line with dx = 10 and dy = 6 (where 0 < m < 1), what is the initial decision parameter P0?","options":["P0 = 2","P0 = 4","P0 = -4","P0 = 16"],"correct":0,"explanation":"معادلة معامل القرار الابتدائي في Bresenham هي: P0 = 2*dy - dx = 2*(6) - 10 = 12 - 10 = 2.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics"},{"id":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics:cg-q5","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: DDA & Bresenham Line","topic":"Bresenham Advantage","question":"Why is Bresenham's line algorithm preferred over the DDA algorithm in hardware implementations?","options":["It uses only integer addition, subtraction, and bit-shifting (multiplication by 2), avoiding floating-point arithmetic","It can draw curves without segments","It does not require a Frame Buffer","It calculates square roots at every pixel"],"correct":0,"explanation":"تتميز خوارزمية Bresenham بأنها تعتمد كلياً على الأعداد الصحيحة (Integer Arithmetic) دون قسمة أو تقريب عشري.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics"},{"id":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics:cg-q6","lectureId":"4","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 4: Midpoint Circle","topic":"Midpoint Circle Symmetry","question":"If the point (3, 7) lies on a circle centered at the origin (0, 0), how many symmetric points in total (including itself) are plotted using Circle Symmetry?","options":["2 points","4 points","8 points","16 points"],"correct":2,"explanation":"تعتمد الدائرة على التماثل الثماني (8-Way Symmetry): (±3, ±7) و (±7, ±3) أي 8 نقاط.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics"},{"id":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics:cg-q7","lectureId":"4","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 4: Midpoint Circle","topic":"Midpoint Circle Decision Parameter","question":"For a circle of radius r = 10 centered at (0, 0), what is the integer initial decision parameter P0 = 1 - r at the starting point (0, 10)?","options":["-9","-10","9","-8"],"correct":0,"explanation":"P0 = 1 - r = 1 - 10 = -9.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics"},{"id":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics:cg-q8","lectureId":"5","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 5: Midpoint Ellipse","topic":"Midpoint Ellipse Region Transition","question":"In the Midpoint Ellipse Algorithm, what condition triggers the transition from Region 1 to Region 2 in the first quadrant?","options":["x == y","2 * ry^2 * x >= 2 * rx^2 * y (where the tangent slope becomes <= -1)","P1 < 0","y == ry"],"correct":1,"explanation":"ننتقل من المنطقة الأولى (Region 1) إلى المنطقة الثانية (Region 2) عندما يصبح ميل المماس مساوياً أو أشد انحداراً من -1، أي عندما يتحقق الشرط: 2 * ry^2 * x >= 2 * rx^2 * y.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=computer-graphics"}],"report-writing":[{"id":"subject.html?id=report-writing:rw-q1","lectureId":"1","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 1: Intro & Audience Analysis","topic":"Technical Writing Purpose","question":"What is the primary goal of Technical Report Writing compared to creative writing?","options":["To entertain the reader using figurative metaphors and suspense","To convey complex technical information clearly, concisely, and accurately to support decision-making","To write as many pages as possible using complex vocabulary","To hide experimental errors from management"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الهدف الأساسي للكتابة الفنية هو نقل المعلومات التقنية بدقة ووضوح وإيجاز لمساعدة القارئ في الفهم واتخاذ القرار.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=report-writing"},{"id":"subject.html?id=report-writing:rw-q2","lectureId":"2","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 2: Report Structure & Tone","topic":"Informative vs Descriptive Abstract","question":"Which type of Abstract includes the actual key findings, numerical results, and main conclusions of the report?","options":["Descriptive Abstract","Informative Abstract","Table of Contents","Appendix Glossary"],"correct":1,"explanation":"الملخص الإخباري (Informative Abstract) يلخص المشكلة والمنهجية وأهم النتائج الرقمية والاستنتاجات، بعكس الملخص الوصفي الذي يكتفي بذكر عناوين الموضوعات.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=report-writing"},{"id":"subject.html?id=report-writing:rw-q3","lectureId":"3","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 3: Visuals, Tables & Graphs","topic":"Tables vs Figures Captions","question":"According to standard technical writing conventions, where should captions be placed for Tables and Figures?","options":["Table captions go ABOVE the table; Figure captions go BELOW the figure","Both Table and Figure captions go inside the footer","Table captions go BELOW the table; Figure captions go ABOVE the figure","Captions are optional in engineering reports"],"correct":0,"explanation":"معيار التوثيق الهندسي العالمي يضع عنوان الجدول (Table Caption) أعلى الجدول، وعنوان الشكل التوضيحي (Figure Caption) أسفل الشكل.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=report-writing"},{"id":"subject.html?id=report-writing:rw-q4","lectureId":"4","lectureLabel":"المحاضرة 4: Citations (IEEE/APA)","topic":"IEEE Citation Style","question":"How are in-text citations formatted in the IEEE referencing style commonly used in Computer Science and Engineering?","options":["(Author, Year) in alphabetical order","Bracketed numbers like [1], [2] numbered in the order they first appear in the text","Superscript Roman numerals at the end of the chapter","Full URLs pasted inside every sentence"],"correct":1,"explanation":"يعتمد نظام IEEE على وضع أرقام بين قوسين مربعين [1]، [2] مرتبة حسب أول ظهور للمرجع داخل النص.","sourceUrl":"subject.html?id=report-writing"}]};
